                                    <item row="0" column="1">
                                     <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditRinexNav4">
                                      <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                       <bool>true</bool>
                                      </property>
                                     </widget>
                                    </item>
                                    <item row="0" column="0">
                                     <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputRinexNavFile4">
                                      <property name="toolTip">
                                       <string>&lt;b&gt;RINEX Navigation File 4:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Selects the input RINEX navigation file.&lt;br&gt; This file contains the broadcast satellite orbit and clocks. It supports RINEX formats 2.11 and 3.00.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Multiple RINEX navigation files can be provided for the case each GNSS data is splitted in different files. gLAB will read all RINEX navigation files and merge the data internally (as if only one file had been provided).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RINEX navigation files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;RINEX Navigation Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Multiple RINEX navigation files can be provided in order to account for single constellation RINEX navigation files, not for multiple day processing (see bullet below).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To process multiple days in a single run, RINEX navigation files from multiple days must be concatenated (in chronological order) with or without header (recommended with header). To concatenate files, use the following command line instruction:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linux/Mac/Cygwin terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;cat file1 file2 file3 ... file N &gt; &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Windows terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;copy /b file1+file2+...+fileN &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;File1, file2, etc, are the input files to be concatenated. &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt; is the resulting file after concatenating all input files into one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note that gLAB does not care about filename or extensions (as gLAB will check that the file contents matches the expected one), so any filename or extension can be used for the concatenated file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                      </property>
                                      <property name="styleSheet">
                                       <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                      </property>
                                      <property name="text">
                                       <string>RINEX Navigation File 4:</string>
                                      </property>
                                     </widget>
                                    </item>
                                   </layout>
                                  </widget>
                                 </item>
