                                 <item row="1" column="0">
                                  <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputClkFile">
                                   <property name="sizePolicy">
                                    <sizepolicy hsizetype="Minimum" vsizetype="Preferred">
                                     <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                                     <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                                    </sizepolicy>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="toolTip">
                                    <string>&lt;b&gt;Precise &lt;b&gt;CLK&lt;/b&gt; clock file&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This file contains the clocks of the satellite at specific times. The clock interpolation degree in the &lt;i&gt;Modelling&lt;/i&gt; section affects the computation of clocks in this mode.&lt;br&gt;CLK files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;Precise Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;CLK files usually end at 23:55 (5 minute interval files) or 23:5).30 (30 second interval files), therefore the last 5 minutes (or 30 seconds) cannot be processed due to the lack of clocks. To avoid this issue, it is necessary to concatenate the CLK file with the next day (see bullet below).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To process multiple days in a single run (or for processing the last epochs in day, as explained in bullet above) CLK files from multiple days must be concatenated (in chronological order) with or without header (recommended with header). To concatenate files, use the following command line instruction:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linux/Mac/Cygwin terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;cat file1 file2 file3 ... file N &gt; &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Windows terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;copy /b file1+file2+...+fileN &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;File1, file2, etc, are the input files to be concatenated. &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt; is the resulting file after concatenating all input files into one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note that gLAB does not care about filename or extensions (as gLAB will check that the file contents matches the expected one), so any filename or extension can be used for the concatenated file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="styleSheet">
                                    <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>CLK File:</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </widget>
                                 </item>
                                 <item row="0" column="0">
                                  <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputSP3OrbitsFile">
                                   <property name="toolTip">
                                    <string>&lt;b&gt;Precise orbit and clocks SP3 file&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This file contains the orbits of the satellite at specific times. The orbit interpolation degree in the &lt;i&gt;Modelling&lt;/i&gt; section affects the computation of orbits in this mode.&lt;br&gt;SP3 files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;Precise Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;SP3 files usually end at 23:45 (15 minute interval files) or 23:55 (5 minute interval files), therefore the last 15 minutes (or 5 minutes) cannot be processed due to the lack of orbits and clocks. To avoid this issue, it is necessary to concatenate the SP3 file with the next day (see bullet below).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To process multiple days in a single run (or for processing the last epochs in day, as explained in bullet above) SP3 files from multiple days must be concatenated (in chronological order) with or without header (recommended with header). To concatenate files, use the following command line instruction:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linux/Mac/Cygwin terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;cat file1 file2 file3 ... file N &gt; &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Windows terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;copy /b file1+file2+...+fileN &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;File1, file2, etc, are the input files to be concatenated. &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt; is the resulting file after concatenating all input files into one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note that gLAB does not care about filename or extensions (as gLAB will check that the file contents matches the expected one), so any filename or extension can be used for the concatenated file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="styleSheet">
                                    <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>SP3 File:</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </widget>
                                 </item>
                                 <item row="0" column="2">
                                  <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonPrecise2Files">
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>...</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </widget>
                                 </item>
                                </layout>
                               </widget>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
