                          <item row="0" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputObservationFile">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;RINEX Observation File&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Selects the input RINEX observation file. This file contains the GNSS measurements for a given station. It supports RINEX formats 2.11 and 3.xx.&lt;br&gt;RINEX Observation files can be found in the links provided in the following menus:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;RINEX Observation Files&lt;br&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;RINEX files from Institutions&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; To process multiple days in a single run, RINEX observation files from multiple days must be concatenated (in chronological order) with or without header (recommended with header). To concatenate files, use the following command line instruction:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linux/Mac/Cygwin terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;cat file1 file2 file3 ... file N &gt; &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Windows terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;copy /b file1+file2+...+fileN &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;File1, file2, etc, are the input files to be concatenated. &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt; is the resulting file after concatenating all input files into one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note that gLAB does not care about filename or extensions (as gLAB will check that the file contents matches the expected one), so any filename or extension can be used for the concatenated file.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>RINEX Observation File:</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="2" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxSatAntex">
                            <property name="sizePolicy">
                             <sizepolicy hsizetype="Minimum" vsizetype="Minimum">
                              <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                              <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                             </sizepolicy>
                            </property>
                            <property name="minimumSize">
                             <size>
                              <width>0</width>
                              <height>23</height>
                             </size>
                            </property>
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;ANTEX File:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Selects the input ANTEX file. This file contains information on the antenna phase centre of the GNSS satellites and ground stations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;ANTEX files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;Other Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; In SPP, SBAS or DGNSS modes, this option can be used to provide gLAB an ANTEX file for reading the satellite blocks (this is need to print the satellite block and SVN in the output messages, as well as removing non existent frequencies and measurements in older satellites from the frequency and measurements priority list).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>ANTEX File:</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                         </layout>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
