                                 <item row="0" column="0">
                                  <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputIonexIonoFile">
                                   <property name="toolTip">
                                    <string>&lt;b&gt;IONEX File:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specify a IONEX file to obtain the iono correction. IONEX multi-layer and variable time between maps are supported. Supported versions are 1.00 and 1.1.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;IONEX files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;Other Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; To process multiple days in a single run, IONEX files from multiple days must be concatenated (in chronological order) with or without header (recommended with header). To concatenate files, use the following command line instruction:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linux/Mac/Cygwin terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;cat file1 file2 file3 ... file N &gt; &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Windows terminal:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;copy /b file1+file2+...+fileN &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;File1, file2, etc, are the input files to be concatenated. &lt;i&gt;Concatenated_file&lt;/i&gt; is the resulting file after concatenating all input files into one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note that gLAB does not care about filename or extensions (as gLAB will check that the file contents matches the expected one), so any filename or extension can be used for the concatenated file.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="styleSheet">
                                    <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                   </property>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>IONEX File:</string>
