                                    <number>6</number>
                                   </property>
                                   <item row="0" column="0">
                                    <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputDCBP1C1File">
                                     <property name="toolTip">
                                      <string>&lt;b&gt;P1-C1 DCB File: &lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specify a file with the GPS P1-C1 Differential Code Bias &lt;b&quot;&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt; corrections. This file is generated by the International GNSS Service (&lt;b&gt;IGS&lt;/b&gt;) and gives an accurate monthly estimation of the GPS (P1-C1) bias for all Satellites. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Because the &lt;font style=&quot; color:#c00000;&quot;&gt;code generation depends on the Receiver Type,&lt;/font&gt; this receiver-related information has to be given (see next field). &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;P1-C1 DCB files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&quot; color:#0000ff;&quot;&gt;Help-&amp;gt;Download data files-&amp;gt;Other Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                     </property>
                                     <property name="styleSheet">
                                      <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                     </property>
                                     <property name="text">
                                      <string>DCB File:</string>
                                     </property>
                                    </widget>
                                   </item>
                                   <item row="0" column="1">
                                    <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditDcbFile">
                                     <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                      <bool>true</bool>
                                     </property>
                                    </widget>
                                   </item>
                                   <item row="0" column="2">
                                    <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonDcbFile">
                                     <property name="text">
                                      <string>...</string>
                                     </property>
                                    </widget>
                                   </item>
                                   <item row="3" column="0" colspan="3">
                                    <widget class="QStackedWidget" name="stackedWidgetGPSReceiverType">
                                     <property name="currentIndex">
                                      <number>1</number>
                                     </property>
                                     <widget class="QWidget" name="page_197">
                                      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_445">
                                       <property name="leftMargin">
                                        <number>0</number>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="topMargin">
                                        <number>0</number>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="rightMargin">
                                        <number>0</number>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="bottomMargin">
                                        <number>0</number>
                                       </property>
                                       <item row="0" column="0">
                                        <widget class="QLabel" name="labelInputGPSRecFile">
                                         <property name="toolTip">
                                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Receiver Type File: &lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specify a receiver type file. This file details naming conventions for IGS equipment, in-site logs, RINEX headers, and SINEX files. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; These naming conventions include manufacturer's name, model and code of: Receivers, Antennas, Radomes, and Antenna+Radome. Additional and historical equipment names also appear. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Because codes are generated differently depending the Receiver Type, C1-P1 biases need to be removed as follows: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 0 &lt;/b&gt; : C1-P1 classification unknown. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 1 &lt;/b&gt; : Cross correlated receiver, reporting: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; C1 &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; P2 = C1 + (Y&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; - Y&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;  Needs Corrections to obtain P1 and a consistent P2: P1=C1+b and P2=P2+b &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;  &lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 2 &lt;/b&gt; : C1 reported in place of P1: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;  Needs Corrections to obtain P1: P1=C1+b  &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 3 &lt;/b&gt; : L1,L2,P1,P2 reported as consistent set: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;  No bias removal needed. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;  &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;GPS Receiver Types files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;Other Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                         </property>
                                         <property name="styleSheet">
                                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                         </property>
                                         <property name="text">
                                          <string>Rec Type File:</string>
                                         </property>
                                        </widget>
                                       </item>
