                          <height>20</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                       </spacer>
                      </item>
                     </layout>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
                   <item row="6" column="0">
                    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxIGF">
                     <property name="toolTip">
                      <string>&lt;b&gt;Iono Geometry-Free carrier phase combination (Triple or Quadruple frequency)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This cycle-slip detector for triple or quadruple frequency receivers uses only carrier phase measurements. The detection is based on fitting a second-degree polynomial with the iono geometry-free combination within a sliding window of &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;N-sample&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The iono geometry-free can be calculated with two methods: using two linearly independent iono-free combinations (see tooltip &lt;i&gt;Two Iono Geometry-Free&lt;/i&gt; below) or with a minimum noise combination (see tooltip &lt;i&gt;Minimum Noise&lt;/i&gt; below).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A cycle-slip is declared when any of the two following statements (OR) is fulfilled:&lt;blockquote&gt;1. If the expected value is larger than the measured one by more than a specific threshold (&lt;i&gt;Th&lt;/i&gt;) &lt;b&gt;AND&lt;/b&gt; also larger than 2 times the residual (&lt;i&gt;res&lt;/i&gt;) of the Least Square (LS) used to fit the second-degree polynomial.&lt;br&gt;The threshold is obtained as:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;Th&lt;/i&gt; = &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;maximum threshold&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; / (1 + exp( -&lt;i&gt;Data Gap&lt;/i&gt; / &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Time constant&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; ))&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Therefore, the conditions to fulfil a cycle-slip are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;| &lt;i&gt;IGF&lt;sub&gt;t&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; - &lt;i&gt;IGF&lt;sub&gt;Estimated&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; | &gt; &lt;i&gt;Th&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;| &lt;i&gt;IGF&lt;sub&gt;t&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; - &lt;i&gt;IGF&lt;sub&gt;Estimated&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; | &gt; 2*&lt;i&gt;res&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. The jump between two consecutive iono geometry-free combinations (IGF) is larger than the &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;maximum jump threshold&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;i&gt;MaxJumpTh&lt;/i&gt;).&lt;br&gt;That is,&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;| &lt;i&gt;IGF&lt;sub&gt;t&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; - &lt;i&gt;IGF&lt;sub&gt;t-1&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; | &gt; &lt;i&gt;MaxJumpTh&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;N-sample&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; is the number of epochs used to fit the second-degree polynomial.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; that&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt; N-sample&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; will be overridden by &lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt;, where:&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt; = maximum( &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Phase-Code difference [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Melbourne-Wübbena [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Geometry-free [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Iono Geometry-free [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt; )&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; When a cycle-slip is detected, the sample will be set as an outlier and ignored. If in the next sample a cycle-slip is also detected, a cycle-slip will be declared. Otherwise, the arc will be maintained. Set option &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Do not declare outliers&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; to disable this behaviour.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                     </property>
                     <property name="styleSheet">
                      <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                     </property>
                     <property name="text">
                      <string>IGF (Triple or Quadruple frequency)</string>
                     </property>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
