                       <item row="1" column="0" colspan="2">
                        <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonSFAutoSelection">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Automatic measurements selection:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;gLAB will automatically select the frequencies and measurements to use. gLAB will select the frequencies and measurements according to the frequency and measurement priority table, which can be set in the menu &lt;i&gt;Set GNSS Frequencies and Measurements Order&lt;/i&gt; available at the FILTER tab.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The number of iterations of this cycle-slip detector will be as much as necessary to cover all carrier phase measurements used in the filter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In case that gLAB cannot create iterations of this cycle-slip detector (due to missing frequencies or measurements in the RINEX observation files or the user has disabled too many frequencies or measurements) an INFO message will be printed with the frequencies not processed by the cycle-slip detector.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In automatic mode, the frequencies and measurements are selected in a per satellite basis, even though in the GUI the frequencies and measurements order can only be selected in a per constellation basis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Automatic measurements selection</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                      </layout>
                     </widget>
                     <widget class="QWidget" name="page_5">
                      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_71">
                       <property name="topMargin">
                        <number>9</number>
                       </property>
                       <property name="bottomMargin">
                        <number>3</number>
                       </property>
                       <item row="2" column="0">
                        <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonMWManualSelection">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Manual measurements selection:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Manually select the frequencies and measurements to use in each iteration of the cycle-slip detector (up to three different iterations). Each iteration corresponds to a MW combination. There are three ways of selecting the frequencies and measurements:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Automatic mode:&lt;/b&gt; Frequencies and measurements are selected by gLAB (the default). In this mode frequencies are set to &quot;Auto&quot; and measurement selection is disabled. Note that when a frequency is manually select, it will automatically switch to semi-automatic mode.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Semi-automatic mode:&lt;/b&gt; The user selects only the frequencies of each iteration, but the measurements are selected by gLAB. To use this mode, select the frequencies and leave the measurements to &quot;Auto&quot;. Note that if any measurement is selected, it will switch automatically to manual mode.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Manual mode:&lt;/b&gt; Select both the frequencies and measurements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the iterations selected do not cover all carrier phase measurements used in the filter, gLAB will add as much iterations as necessary. It is possible to disable this behaviour with the command line switch '-pre:cs:mw:noautofill' (for MW detector only) or with '-pre:cs:noautofill' (for all cycle-slip detectors).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In the GUI, each iteration applies to all satellites of a constellation with a maximum of 3 iterations. In command line, it is possible to provide different number of iterations (with different frequency and measurement combination) in a per satellite basis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Manual measurements selection</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="3" column="0">
                        <spacer name="verticalSpacer_63">
                         <property name="orientation">
                          <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                          <size>
                           <width>20</width>
                           <height>0</height>
                          </size>
                         </property>
                        </spacer>
