                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="0" colspan="3">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxLINoOutliers">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Do not declare outliers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;After filling the cycle-slip sample buffer, the first time the cycle-slip detector triggers, instead of declaring a cycle-slip, an outlier is declared. When an outlier is declared, the sample is skipped and waits for the next epoch. If in the next epoch the cycle-slip detector triggers again, a cycle-slip is declared. Otherwise, the arc continues (but the sample declared as outlier is skipped).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This technique is useful for trying to make arcs longer, as sometimes only a single bad sample (an outlier) is given in a continuous arc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enable this option to disable gLAB behaviour to declare outliers (therefore any time the cycle-slip triggers a cycle-slip will be declared).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; An outlier sample does not count as a data gap.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Do not declare outliers</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                         </layout>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="2" column="0" colspan="2">
                        <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonLIAutoSelection">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Automatic measurements selection:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;gLAB will automatically select the frequencies and measurements to use. gLAB will select the frequencies and measurements according to the frequency and measurement priority table, which can be set in the menu &lt;i&gt;Set GNSS Frequencies and Measurements Order&lt;/i&gt; available at the FILTER tab.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The number of iterations of this cycle-slip detector will be as much as necessary to cover all carrier phase measurements used in the filter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In case that gLAB cannot create iterations of this cycle-slip detector (due to missing frequencies or measurements in the RINEX observation files or the user has disabled too many frequencies or measurements) an INFO message will be printed with the frequencies not processed by the cycle-slip detector.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In automatic mode, the frequencies and measurements are selected in a per satellite basis, even though in the GUI the frequencies and measurements order can only be selected in a per constellation basis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Automatic measurements selection</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                      </layout>
                     </widget>
                     <widget class="QWidget" name="page_11">
                      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_524">
                       <property name="topMargin">
                        <number>9</number>
                       </property>
                       <property name="bottomMargin">
                        <number>3</number>
                       </property>
                       <item row="4" column="0">
                        <spacer name="verticalSpacer_62">
                         <property name="orientation">
                          <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                          <size>
                           <width>20</width>
                           <height>0</height>
                          </size>
                         </property>
                        </spacer>
                       </item>
                       <item row="3" column="0">
                        <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonIGFManualSelection">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Manual measurements selection:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Manually select the frequencies and measurements to use in each iteration of the cycle-slip detector (up to three different iterations). Each iteration corresponds to an IGF combination. There are three ways of selecting the frequencies and measurements:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Automatic mode:&lt;/b&gt; Frequencies and measurements are selected by gLAB (the default). In this mode frequencies are set to &quot;Auto&quot; and measurement selection is disabled. Note that when a frequency is manually select, it will automatically switch to semi-automatic mode.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Semi-automatic mode:&lt;/b&gt; The user selects only the frequencies of each iteration, but the measurements are selected by gLAB. To use this mode, select the frequencies and leave the measurements to &quot;Auto&quot;. Note that if any measurement is selected, it will switch automatically to manual mode.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Manual mode:&lt;/b&gt; Select both the frequencies and measurements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the iterations selected do not cover all carrier phase measurements used in the filter, gLAB will add as much iterations as necessary. It is possible to disable this behaviour with the command line switch '-pre:cs:igf:noautofill' (for IGF detector only) or with '-pre:cs:noautofill' (for all cycle-slip detectors).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In the GUI, each iteration applies to all satellites of a constellation with a maximum of 3 iterations. In command line, it is possible to provide different number of iterations (with different frequency and measurement combination) in a per satellite basis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Manual measurements selection</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="3" column="1">
                        <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonIGFSelectMeasurements">
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Select Measurements</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="0" column="0" colspan="2">
                        <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxIGF">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>75</weight>
                           <bold>true</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="title">
                          <string>IGF Cycle-slip Detection Parameters</string>
                         </property>
                         <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_523">
                          <property name="topMargin">
                           <number>9</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="bottomMargin">
                           <number>3</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="verticalSpacing">
                           <number>3</number>
                          </property>
                          <item row="5" column="2">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_317">
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>(s)</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="2">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_315">
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>(m)</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="3" column="1">
                           <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditIGFmaxJumpThreshold">
                            <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="5" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_311">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Time Constant&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the time constant (in seconds) of the threshold computed in the formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Th&lt;/i&gt; = &lt;i&gt;maximum threshold&lt;/i&gt; / (1 + exp( -&lt;i&gt;Data Gap&lt;/i&gt; / &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Time constant&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; ))&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Time Constant</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="6" column="2">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_318">
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>(epochs)</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="1">
                           <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditIGFmaxThreshold">
                            <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="6" column="1">
                           <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditIGFnSamples">
                            <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="3" column="2">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_316">
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>(m)</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="3" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_194">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Maximum Jump Threshold&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the maximum difference (in meters) between two consecutive iono geometry-free combinations (IGF). If this value is surpassed, a cycle-slip will be declared.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Maximum Jump Threshold</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="5" column="1">
                           <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditIGFtimeConstant">
                            <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="3">
                           <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_87">
                            <property name="orientation">
                             <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                            </property>
                            <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                             <size>
                              <width>0</width>
                              <height>20</height>
                             </size>
                            </property>
                           </spacer>
                          </item>
                          <item row="1" column="0" colspan="3">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxIGFNoOutliers">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Do not declare outliers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;After filling the cycle-slip sample buffer, the first time the cycle-slip detector triggers, instead of declaring a cycle-slip, an outlier is declared. When an outlier is declared, the sample is skipped and waits for the next epoch. If in the next epoch the cycle-slip detector triggers again, a cycle-slip is declared. Otherwise, the arc continues (but the sample declared as outlier is skipped).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This technique is useful for trying to make arcs longer, as sometimes only a single bad sample (an outlier) is given in a continuous arc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enable this option to disable gLAB behaviour to declare outliers (therefore any time the cycle-slip triggers a cycle-slip will be declared).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; An outlier sample does not count as a data gap.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Do not declare outliers</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="6" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_313">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;N-sample&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimum number of samples to consider that the cycle-slip detector is active. It must be equal or greater than 2. Until N-samples+1 are available, the satellite will be discarded.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; If more than one cycle-slip detector is enabled, then N-sample will have the following value:&lt;br&gt;N-sample = maximum( &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Phase-Code difference [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Melbourne-Wübbena [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Geometry-free [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;N-sample of Iono Geometry-free [if enabled]&lt;/i&gt; )&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>N-sample</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_314">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Maximum Threshold&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the upper bound value (in metres) of the threshold computed in the formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Th&lt;/i&gt; = &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;maximum threshold&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; / (1 + exp( -&lt;i&gt;Data Gap&lt;/i&gt; / &lt;i&gt;Time constant&lt;/i&gt; ))&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Maximum Threshold</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="2" column="0" colspan="3">
                           <widget class="QFrame" name="frame_48">
                            <property name="frameShape">
                             <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                            </property>
                            <property name="frameShadow">
                             <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_596">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="verticalSpacing">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonIGFMinimumNoise">
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Minimum Noise combination:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Construct a iono geometry-free combination with three frequencies using the following combination:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;IGF = &amp;alpha;·L1 + &amp;beta;·L2 + &amp;gamma;·L3&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;alpha;, &amp;beta; and &amp;gamma; are computed by gLAB (and printed in IGFCSDATA message) with the following formulas:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;alpha; + &amp;beta; + &amp;gamma; = 0&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;alpha;·&amp;lambda;1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; + &amp;beta;·&amp;lambda;2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; + &amp;gamma;·&amp;lambda;3&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = 0&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;alpha; &gt; 0&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;alpha;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; + &amp;beta;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; + &amp;gamma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = 1&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;L1, L2 and L3 are the carrier phases of three different frequencies, while &amp;lambda;1, &amp;lambda;2 and &amp;lambda;3 are the wavelength of the respective carrier phases.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Combining this formulas, the following equations result to compute &amp;alpha;, &amp;beta; and &amp;gamma;:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;alpha; = (&amp;lambda;3&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - &amp;lambda;2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;) / N&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;beta; = (&amp;lambda;1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - &amp;lambda;3&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;) / N&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;gamma; = (&amp;lambda;2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - &amp;lambda;1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;) / N&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;N =  (&amp;lambda;3&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - &amp;lambda;2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; +   (&amp;lambda;1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - &amp;lambda;3&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; + (&amp;lambda;2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - &amp;lambda;1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This combination provides the iono geometry-free combination with minimum noise, but has the side effect that some frequencies will have a small weight in the combination (due to any of the factor &amp;alpha;, &amp;beta; or &amp;gamma; being much smaller than other of the factors), potentially hiding a single cycle cycle-slip in the combination.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This combination has been extracted from &lt;i&gt;The System: Three’s the Challenge&lt;/i&gt; (Oliver Montenbruck et al), available at &lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;https://www.gpsworld.com/threes-challenge/&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt; </string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="styleSheet">
                                <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>Minimum Noise</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                             <item row="0" column="1">
                              <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonIGFTwoIonoFree">
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Two Iono Geometry-free combinations:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Two linearly independent Geometry-free combinations are computed and then subtracted to each other. The remaining contents are the ambiguities and wind-up. These dual geometry-free combination can be computed using three or four different frequencies (by default three frequencies are used).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="styleSheet">
                                <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>Two Iono Geometry-Free</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                             <item row="0" column="2">
                              <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_124">
                               <property name="orientation">
                                <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                <size>
                                 <width>40</width>
                                 <height>20</height>
                                </size>
                               </property>
                              </spacer>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                         </layout>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="2" column="0" colspan="2">
                        <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonIGFAutoSelection">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Automatic measurements selection:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;gLAB will automatically select the frequencies and measurements to use. gLAB will select the frequencies and measurements according to the frequency and measurement priority table, which can be set in the menu &lt;i&gt;Set GNSS Frequencies and Measurements Order&lt;/i&gt; available at the FILTER tab.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The number of iterations of this cycle-slip detector will be as much as necessary to cover all carrier phase measurements used in the filter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In case that gLAB cannot create iterations of this cycle-slip detector (due to missing frequencies or measurements in the RINEX observation files or the user has disabled too many frequencies or measurements) an INFO message will be printed with the frequencies not processed by the cycle-slip detector.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In automatic mode, the frequencies and measurements are selected in a per satellite basis, even though in the GUI the frequencies and measurements order can only be selected in a per constellation basis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Automatic measurements selection</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                      </layout>
                     </widget>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
                  </layout>
                 </widget>
                </item>
                <item row="0" column="0">
                 <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxStationData">
                  <property name="sizePolicy">
                   <sizepolicy hsizetype="Preferred" vsizetype="Fixed">
                    <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                    <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                   </sizepolicy>
                  </property>
                  <property name="font">
                   <font>
                    <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                    <weight>75</weight>
                    <bold>true</bold>
                   </font>
                  </property>
                  <property name="styleSheet">
                   <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                  </property>
                  <property name="title">
                   <string>Station Data</string>
                  </property>
                  <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_49">
                   <property name="sizeConstraint">
                    <enum>QLayout::SetDefaultConstraint</enum>
                   </property>
                   <property name="topMargin">
                    <number>9</number>
                   </property>
                   <property name="bottomMargin">
                    <number>6</number>
                   </property>
                   <property name="verticalSpacing">
                    <number>3</number>
                   </property>
                   <item row="0" column="1">
                    <widget class="QFrame" name="frameDataDecimator">
                     <property name="frameShape">
                      <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                     </property>
                     <property name="frameShadow">
                      <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                     </property>
                     <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_161">
                      <property name="leftMargin">
                       <number>0</number>
                      </property>
                      <property name="topMargin">
                       <number>0</number>
                      </property>
                      <property name="rightMargin">
                       <number>0</number>
                      </property>
                      <property name="bottomMargin">
                       <number>0</number>
                      </property>
                      <item row="0" column="0">
                       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditDataDecimator">
                        <property name="maximumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>80</width>
                          <height>16777215</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="0" column="1">
                       <widget class="QLabel" name="label_167">
                        <property name="styleSheet">
                         <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>(s)</string>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                     </layout>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
                   <item row="1" column="0" colspan="2">
                    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxReceiverCodeJumps">
                     <property name="toolTip">
                      <string>&lt;b&gt;Check for jumps in code measurements&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Some receivers do not output a set of physically consistent measurements. When they adjust their clock, a &quot;jump&quot; should appear both in pseudorange and carrier-phase measurements, but it only appears in pseudorange. This creates a massive cycle-slip for all satellites in this epoch if it is not corrected.&lt;br&gt;If this option is enabled, gLAB will detect and correct this behaviour, providing a set of consistent observables.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                     </property>
                     <property name="styleSheet">
                      <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                     </property>
                     <property name="text">
                      <string>Check for jumps in code measurements</string>
                     </property>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
                   <item row="0" column="0">
                    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxDataDecimator">
                     <property name="minimumSize">
                      <size>
                       <width>0</width>
                       <height>23</height>
                      </size>
                     </property>
                     <property name="font">
                      <font>
                       <weight>50</weight>
                       <bold>false</bold>
                      </font>
                     </property>
                     <property name="toolTip">
                      <string>&lt;b&gt;Data decimation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mark this option to decimate the input data at the specified rate [in seconds] (rate can be decimal, up to 0.0001 seconds resolution).&lt;br&gt;If this option is unchecked, every time an epoch is found in the input RINEX observation file, all the processing takes place.&lt;br&gt;If this option is checked, the data is decimated and not even modelled. Even in decimated data, all the epochs are used for cycle-slip detection, and arc length computations, but the process is stopped just before the modelling.&lt;br&gt;This option is meant to be used to reduce computation time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; If decimation is higher than one second the decimation value will be truncated to avoid problems with decimals.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                     </property>
                     <property name="styleSheet">
                      <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                     </property>
                     <property name="text">
                      <string>Data Decimation</string>
                     </property>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
