                          </item>
                          <item row="2" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="labelNavTypeGalileo">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Galileo&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the priority order for Galileo navigation message selection. The selected navigation messages will be used for computing orbits and clocks. See &lt;i&gt;Preferred age time&lt;/i&gt; below for details on the navigation message selection algorithm.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The navigation message types supported for Galileo are:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;FNAV:&lt;/b&gt; Free navigation message sent in E5a signal. F/NAV dock correction is referred to the E1-E5a combination.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;I/NAV E1:&lt;/b&gt; Integrity navigation message sent in E1-B signal. I/NAV dock correction is referred to the E1-E5b combination.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;I/NAV E5b:&lt;/b&gt; Integrity navigation message sent in E5b signal. I/NAV dock correction is referred to the E1-E5b combination.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;I/NAV E1E5b:&lt;/b&gt; Integrity navigation message merging the info from E1-B and E5b signals. I/NAV dock correction is referred to the E1-E5b combination.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; The only difference between I/NAV E1, I/NAV E5b and I/NAV E1E5b in the RINEX navigation file are the health and validity status flags. I/NAV E1 only has the flags for E1, I/NAV E5b for E5b and  I/NAV E1E5b for both E1 and E5b.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Galileo</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
