                       <item row="1" column="0">
                        <widget class="QFrame" name="frameNavFreshTime">
                         <property name="sizePolicy">
                          <sizepolicy hsizetype="Preferred" vsizetype="Minimum">
                           <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                           <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                          </sizepolicy>
                         </property>
                         <property name="frameShape">
                          <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="frameShadow">
                          <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                         </property>
                         <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_206">
                          <property name="leftMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="topMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="rightMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="bottomMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <item row="0" column="0">
                           <widget class="QLabel" name="labelNavFreshTime">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Preferred age time:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When searching for a navigation message, set the threshold (in seconds) to decide if current valid navigation message found is recent enough (with respect to navigation message ToC -Time of Clock-) to select it or to keep searching in other navigation message types (according to the navigation message priority list) for more recent messages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The navigation message selection algorithm is the following:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Select the navigation message type with higher priority.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Loop through the navigation messages and find the one with closest ToE (Time of Ephemerides) and valid transmission time (if &lt;i&gt;Check Broadcast Transmission Time&lt;/i&gt; is enabled).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check if difference between ToC (Time of Clock) and current is less than the value provided in &lt;i&gt;Preferred age time&lt;/i&gt; (this parameter). If it is smaller, the algorithm ends. If it is greater, repeat steps 1 to 3 with the next navigation message in the priority type list.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If valid navigation messages are found but none of them are below the &lt;i&gt;Preferred age time&lt;/i&gt;  ToC difference, the navigation message with smaller ToC difference will be selected.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the value of this parameter is set very small (e.g. 1 second), this will make gLAB to loop through all available navigation message types in nearly all cases, as very rarely any navigation message will meet the condition.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the value of this parameter is set very high (e.g. 4 hours), gLAB will use the navigation message found in the first navigation type (even though it may be very old), as any navigation message will meet the condition.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;When a navigation message is searched by IOD (Issue Of Data) -which occurs in SBAS modes- the same algorithm applies, but only looping on the navigation messages with the given IOD (there may be more than one when concatenating multiple RINEX navigation files), as the navigation messages are also internally saved by IOD.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Navigation message health check is not performed in this algorithm, it is checked after a navigation message is selected (according to &lt;i&gt;Discard Unhealthy Satellites&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;Discard Marginal Satellites&lt;/i&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In command line, there are the advanced options '-model:skipunhealthy' and '-model:skipunhealthymarg' which makes gLAB to skip unhealthy or unhealthy and marginal navigation message from the RINEX navigation files (i.e. not saving them in memory), so gLAB will only run the navigation selection algorithm with healthy and marginal or healthy only navigation messages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Preferred age time:</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="1">
                           <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditNavFreshTime">
