                       </item>
                       <item row="1" column="0">
                        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_93">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Navigation Mode&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Select the initial navigation mode for SBAS.&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;PA (Precission Approach):&lt;/b&gt; This is the default mode. It guarantees integrity in navigation and maximum precission (around 1 metre). In order to be able to use a satellite for navigation in PA mode, all the SBAS conditions for fast, slow and ionosphere corrections must be fulfilled. If navigation mode switching is enabled, gLAB will switch to NPA mode when there are less than 4 satellites available for navigation and GEO switch is not possible.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;NPA (Non Precission Approach):&lt;/b&gt; This mode does not guarantee integrity or precission, and can be used in non critical operations. In this mode, if fast or slow corrections are not available, it will not use them (but it will set a sigma for these of 60 metres). If ionosphere correction is not available, it will use GPS Klobuchar model instead with a large sigma. If no corrections at all are available, navigation will be equal to SPP mode, but with sigmas larger than 60 metres). If this mode is set as the initial mode, it will be maintained during all the processing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Navigation Mode</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="4" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxGEOexclusion">
                         <property name="minimumSize">
                          <size>
                           <width>0</width>
                           <height>23</height>
                          </size>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;GEO Exclusion&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When a GEO is excluded, its data will not be read (as if there were no messages in the data file). This option is useful if we want to exclude GEOs sending alarm messages continuosly, or avoid switching to GEOs that are in test mode.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; In the GUI, the maximum number of GEO to be excluded is three, but in command line, it is possible to exclude any number of GEO by providing the parameter '-pre:geoexclude' as many times as necessary or by providing a comma separated list of GEO to the same parameter.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>GEO Exclusion</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
