                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="5" column="0">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_416">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;OBAD Parameters and DFREI Scale Table&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message type 37. This message sends the common (all constellation) OBAD (Old But Active Data) parameters (I&lt;sub&gt;VALID&lt;/sub&gt;, C&lt;sub&gt;ER&lt;/sub&gt;, C&lt;sub&gt;COVARIANCE&lt;/sub&gt;) and three OBAD parameters (I&lt;sub&gt;CORR&lt;/sub&gt;, C&lt;sub&gt;CORR&lt;/sub&gt;, R&lt;sub&gt;CORR&lt;/sub&gt;) for each constellation. These parameters are used for computing the degradation parameters for &amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFC&lt;/sub&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message type 37 also sends the conversion table for each value of the DFREI (Dual Frequency Range Error Indicator) to &amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt; in metres (for DFREI values from 0 to 14, as value 15 means to not use the satellite).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>OBAD Parameters and
DFREI Scale Table</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="0" column="1">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_485">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;MT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message Type number defined in MOPS.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>MT</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="alignment">
                                 <set>Qt::AlignCenter</set>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="1" column="1">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_383">
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>0</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="alignment">
                                 <set>Qt::AlignCenter</set>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="5" column="2">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditOBADParDFREITablePA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="6" column="0">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_151">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;SBAS Satellite Ephemeris Corrections and Covariance Matrix&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Messages type 39 and 40 send a full set of Keplerian parameters, along with the covariance matrix parameters.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This message is only sent for the SBAS satellite sending the corrections (it uses this message instead of message type 32 -&lt;i&gt;Clock Ephemeris Corrections and Covariance Matrix&lt;/i&gt;-) and only if it is providing ranging service. If no ranging service is provided, then no message type 32, 39 or 40 is sent for the SBAS satellite sending the corrections.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; As messages type 39 and 40 send a full set of Keplerian parameters, it allows to handle different types of orbits, like IGSO (Inclined Geo-Synchronous Orbit), HEO (High Earth Orbit), MEO (Medium Earth Orbit) or GEO (Geostationary Earth Orbit).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>SBAS Satellite Ephemeris
Corrections and
Covariance Matrix</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="0" column="2">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_SBAS_PA_timeouts_DFMC">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;PA&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Time-out values (in seconds) in PA (Precision Approach) navigation mode.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; The condition to check if a message has time-out for any message (except for range rate corrections) is:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(t - t&lt;sub&gt;lastbit&lt;/sub&gt;) &gt; t&lt;sub&gt;max&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;t:&lt;/b&gt; The current epoch.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;t&lt;sub&gt;lastbit&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Time of reception of last bit of current message (taking into account the 0.1 seconds of signal travel time).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;t&lt;sub&gt;max&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The time-out value for the current message and navigation mode.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>PA</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="alignment">
                                 <set>Qt::AlignCenter</set>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="4" column="1">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_486">
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>34/35/36</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="alignment">
                                 <set>Qt::AlignCenter</set>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="4" column="0">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_488">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;Integrity Messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Integrity corrections are given in messages type 34, 35 and 36. Messages type 34, 35, and 36 send DFRECI (Dual Frequency Range Error Change Indicator) for all satellites in the mask (92 DFRECI) and 7 DFREI (Dual Frequency Range Error Indicator). DFREI value is used to get the &amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt; using a conversion table sent in message type 37 (&lt;i&gt;OBAD Parameters and DFREI Scale Table&lt;/i&gt;).&lt;br&gt;DFRECI is a flag to indicate if the DFREI has changed, occupies 2 bits each and can have the following values:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;0:&lt;/b&gt; DFREI has not changed (only when 0 &amp;le; DFREI &amp;le; 14).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1:&lt;/b&gt; DFREI value is changed (only when 0 &amp;le; new DFREI &amp;le; 14), and that the corresponding new DFREI value is transmitted within the DFREI section of the message (type 34).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2:&lt;/b&gt; DFREI is increased by 1 index (bump) (if the current DFREI value is 15, then the bumped DFREI value remains at 15).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite corresponding to the Augmented Slot Index is set to &quot;Not for use in SBAS mode&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Messages type 35 and 36 just send the DFREI values for all satellites. Message type 35 sends DFREI for slots 1 to 53, while message type 36 sends DFREI for slots 54 to 92.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message type 34 is used to reduce bandwidth, as in many cases DFREI values on satellites will not change all at the same time. If 7 or less satellite DFREI change at a given time (changes different from being increased by 1), a message type 34 is enough to refresh all satellites sigmas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Moreover, DFREI is also sent within message type 32 (&lt;i&gt;Clock Ephemeris Corrections and Covariance Matrix&lt;/i&gt;), which can be used to refresh a few more DFREI along with MT34 if time constraints are met. Otherwise, messages type 35 and 36 are sent with new DFREI values of all satellites. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All three messages type 34, 35 and 36 send an IODM which must match with the one sent in message type 31 (&lt;i&gt;Satellite Mask&lt;/i&gt;), otherwise these messages cannot be decoded.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DFC (Dual Frequency Corrections) sigma is computed with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;DFC&lt;/sub&gt; = ( &amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt; · &amp;delta;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt; )&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; + &amp;epsilon;&lt;sub&gt;corr&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; +  &amp;epsilon;&lt;sub&gt;er&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The sigma provided through DFREI parameters in MT 34/35/36.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;delta;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Factor dependent on user location computed from the covariance matrix, which is broadcast in MT 32 or MT 40 (the latter only for the SBAS satellite broadcasting the correction and integrity data in use).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;epsilon;&lt;sub&gt;corr&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Degradation parameter for the SBAS DFMC corrections.&lt;li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;epsilon;&lt;sub&gt;er&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Degradation parameter for NPA (Non Precision Approach) applications.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>Integrity Messages</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="3" column="3">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditClkCovarianceMatrixNPA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="6" column="4">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_492">
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>(s)</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="7" column="3">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditTimeOffsetsNPA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="6" column="3">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditSatCovarianceMatrixNPA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="2" column="0">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_365">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;Satellite Mask&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message type 31. This message has 214 ordered slots, each one corresponding to a given satellite PRN and constellation. Each slot is one bit, if the bit is 1, the satellite is monitored, otherwise the satellite is not monitored. This set of ordered slots is called the PRN mask. The order is important, as the order of the monitored satellites in the mask will be the order in which the corrections will be sent in other messages. Currently, the slots are assigned in the following way:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 1- 37:&lt;/b&gt; For GPS satellites. Slots 33 to 37 are GPS reserved slots.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 38- 74:&lt;/b&gt; For GLONASS satellites (GLONASS PRN +37).  Slots 70 to 74 are GLONASS reserved slots.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 75- 111:&lt;/b&gt; For Galileo satellites (Galileo PRN +74).  Slot 111 is Galileo reserved slot.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 112- 119:&lt;/b&gt; Spare bits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 120- 158:&lt;/b&gt; For SBAS satellites (bit slot matches SBAS GEO PRN).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 159- 195:&lt;/b&gt; For BeiDou satellites (BeiDou PRN +158).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slots 196- 214:&lt;/b&gt; For future GNSS satellites.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Each message has an IODM (Issue Of Data Mask), which identifies each mask. If any bits of the mask changes, the IODM will change (which will be rare).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The maximum number of concurrent monitored satellites is 92 (including all constellations), due to the limited space in the SBAS messages. Mask messages with more than 92 satellites monitored will be rejected by gLAB.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;All messages that need a mask (to get the order for the satellite corrections), they will also have an IODM associated. Thence, the user must have the mask with the given IODM in order to read the message.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;When a mask change occurs (a mask with a different IODM), the user will have to save the previous mask and also all messages associated to the old IODM until new corrections with the new IODM are received or the old corrections time-out. This assures that a mask transition is smooth and there is continuity of corrections. In practice, SBAS providers usually prefer to send alarm messages during some minutes when a mask change occurs, to force the user clear all the data and switch to another GEO.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>Satellite Mask</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="8" column="2">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditSBASSatAlmanacsPA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="8" column="3">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditSBASSatAlmanacsNPA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="0" column="3">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_SBAS_NPA_timeouts_DFMC">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;NPA&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Time-out values (in seconds) in NPA (Non Precision Approach) navigation mode.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; The condition to check if a message has time-out for any message (except for range rate corrections) is:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(t - t&lt;sub&gt;lastbit&lt;/sub&gt;) &gt; t&lt;sub&gt;max&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;t:&lt;/b&gt; The current epoch.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;t&lt;sub&gt;lastbit&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Time of reception of last bit of current message (taking into account the 0.1 seconds of signal travel time).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;t&lt;sub&gt;max&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The time-out value for the current message and navigation mode.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>NPA</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="alignment">
                                 <set>Qt::AlignCenter</set>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="7" column="4">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_401">
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>(s)</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="2" column="2">
                               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEditSatMaskPA_DFMC">
                                <property name="clearButtonEnabled">
                                 <bool>true</bool>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="7" column="0">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_487">
                                <property name="toolTip">
                                 <string>&lt;b&gt;GNSS Time Offsets&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message type 42. This message contains time parameters to synchronize each constellation time and UTC to SNT (SBAS Network Time). It is decoded but not used in gLAB, as time is set by the RINEX observation file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; This message was defined in ED-259 v0.3, but later undefined (set as &lt;i&gt;reserved&lt;/i&gt;) in ED-259 v0.9.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>GNSS Time Offsets</string>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="6" column="1">
                               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_434">
                                <property name="styleSheet">
                                 <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>39/40</string>
                                </property>
                                <property name="alignment">
                                 <set>Qt::AlignCenter</set>
                                </property>
                               </widget>
                              </item>
                              <item row="0" column="0">
