                          </property>
                          <item row="4" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxAllowKlobucharIono">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Allow Klobuchar Ionosphere During Coordinate Convergence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If receiver position is set to &lt;i&gt;Calculate&lt;/i&gt;  (see &lt;i&gt;A Priori Receiver Position From&lt;/i&gt; in the Input section), gLAB will need to compute the receiver coordinates, starting from the Earth's surface, or the RINEX observation position or the user provided coordinates. In either case, it will probably occur that during the coordinate convergence, the ionosphere pierce points of the satellites are out of the coverage area of the current SBAS provider. In this case, if navigation mode switching is disabled (which is the default), no satellites will be available due to the lack of ionosphere, so no solution will be computed.&lt;br&gt;To overcome this issue, during the convergence of the coordinates, Klobuchar ionosphere model will be allowed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This option also applies when using SBAS ionosphere model but without SBAS processing (e.g. SPP with SBAS ionosphere).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The coordinates are considered to be converged when the current solution and the previous one differ in less than 100 metres.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Allow Klobuchar Ionosphere During Coordinate Convergence</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="14" column="0">
