                                      <string>&lt;b&gt;DFREI=2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the conversion value to metres for DFREI (Dual Frequency Range Error Indicator) equal to 2, ignoring the conversion formula defined in MT37 (explained below).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When DFREI conversion value is read from MT37 (&lt;i&gt;OBAD Parameters and DFREI Scale Table&lt;/i&gt;), the conversion to metres is done with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt; = &amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFREI=2&lt;/sub&gt; · Scale_factor + Min_Range (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;;&amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFREI=2&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Conversion value read from MT37 DFREI table when DFREI=2.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scale_factor:&lt;/b&gt; Scale factor set in ED-259. For DFREI=2, the scale factor is 0.125 (metres)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Min_Range:&lt;/b&gt; Minimum value set in ED-259. For DFREI=2, the minimum value is 0.375 (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;To get the default value set in this option, &amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFREI=2&lt;/sub&gt;=8 is used (&amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFREI&lt;/sub&gt; size is 4 bit, therefore 8 is the intermidiate value between 0 and 15). Applying the formula above:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sub&gt;DFRE&lt;/sub&gt; = 8 ·  0.125 + 0.375 = 1.375 (metres)&lt;br&gt;</string>
