                        <number>6</number>
                       </property>
                       <item row="11" column="0" colspan="2">
                        <widget class="QFrame" name="frame_12">
                         <property name="maximumSize">
                          <size>
                           <width>16777215</width>
                           <height>118</height>
                          </size>
                         </property>
                         <property name="frameShape">
                          <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="frameShadow">
                          <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                         </property>
                         <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_75">
                          <property name="leftMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="topMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="rightMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="bottomMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="verticalSpacing">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <item row="1" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxTropoCorrection">
                            <property name="sizePolicy">
                             <sizepolicy hsizetype="Minimum" vsizetype="Minimum">
                              <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                              <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                             </sizepolicy>
                            </property>
                            <property name="minimumSize">
                             <size>
                              <width>0</width>
                              <height>24</height>
                             </size>
                            </property>
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <weight>50</weight>
                              <bold>false</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Tropospheric correction&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Troposphere is the atmospheric layer placed between Earth’s surface and an altitude of about 60 kilometres. The effect of the troposphere on the GNSS signals appears as an extra delay in the measurement of the signal travelling from the satellite to receiver. This delay depends on the temperature, pressure, humidity as well as the transmitter and receiver antennas location. Because at the frequency which the GPS signal is emitted the troposphere behaves like a non dispersive media, its effect independent of the frequency. The tropospheric delay can be modelled in an approximate way (about 90%-95%) using the following expression:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; T ( elev ) = T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; · M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) + T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; · M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev )&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where it is separately computed:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tropospheric Nominals&lt;/b&gt;: T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; and  T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;: The Tropospheric dry and wet nominal component. It can be divided in hydrostatic, i.e., Dry gases (mainly N&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; and O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; ), and wet, i.e., Water vapour.&lt;br&gt;gLAB implements the following models:&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;UNB-3 Nominal:&lt;/b&gt; The model implemented in SBAS (defined in MOPS). It computes wet and dry components using the receiver height and a fixed table of meteorological parameters. Used in SPP/SBAS/DGNSS.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Simple Nominal:&lt;/b&gt; The tropospheric model implemented in GIPSY-OASIS II software [Webb and Zumberge, 1993]. The dry component is computed with a fixed formula, while the wet component is estimated in the filter. Used in PPP.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tropospheric Mappings&lt;/b&gt;: M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) and M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) : The Tropospheric dry and wet mappings. The tropospheric delay depends on the signal path through the neutral atmosphere, and thence, can be modelled as a function of the satellite elevation angle.&lt;br&gt;gLAB implements the following mappings:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Simple Mapping:&lt;/b&gt; The mapping function is common for both the dry and wet components. It is computed according to the SBAS MOPS. To be used with &lt;i&gt;UNB-3 Nominal&lt;/i&gt; model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Niell Mapping:&lt;/b&gt; Uses two different mapping function for wet and dry components, which are computed with a fixed table of coefficients, as described in [Niell, 1996]. To be used with &lt;i&gt;Simple Nominal&lt;/i&gt; model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The effect of troposphere can range up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;10 m&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Tropospheric Correction</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxIonoCorrection">
                            <property name="sizePolicy">
                             <sizepolicy hsizetype="Minimum" vsizetype="Minimum">
                              <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                              <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                             </sizepolicy>
                            </property>
                            <property name="minimumSize">
                             <size>
                              <width>0</width>
                              <height>24</height>
                             </size>
                            </property>
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <weight>50</weight>
                              <bold>false</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Ionospheric correction&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ionosphere is the zone of the terrestrial atmosphere that extends itself from about 60 km until more than 2000 km high. Due to the interaction with free electrons, electromagnetic signals that go through it suffer a delay/advancement in relation to the propagation in a vacuum. This effect is a dispersive effect (depend on the frequency), and can be removed in multi-frequency receivers (with a specific combination of measurements). The ionosphere models supported by gLAB are:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klobuchar (GPS):&lt;/b&gt; Defined in the GPS ICD, it uses eight parameters broadcasted in the GPS navigation message (in RINEX v2, in the header records &lt;b&gt;ION ALPHA&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;ION BETA&lt;/b&gt;; in RINEX v3, in the header record  &lt;b&gt;IONOSPHERIC CORR&lt;/b&gt; -with the preambles &lt;b&gt;GPSA&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;GPSB&lt;/b&gt;-. It can only reduce its impact between a 50% and a 60%.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;NeQuick (Galileo):&lt;/b&gt; Defined in the Galileo ICD, it uses three parameters broadcast in the Galileo navigation message (in RINEX v3, in the header record IONOSPHERIC CORR -with the preamble GAL-. It can only reduce its impact between a 50% and a 70%.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klobuchar (BeiDou-2):&lt;/b&gt; Defined in the BeiDou-2 ICD, it uses eight parameters broadcasted in the BeiDou-2 navigation message (in RINEX v3, in the header record  &lt;b&gt;IONOSPHERIC CORR&lt;/b&gt; -with the preambles &lt;b&gt;BDSA&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;BDSB&lt;/b&gt;-. It can only reduce its impact between a 50% and a 60%.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;IONEX:&lt;/b&gt; IONEX (IONosphere map EXchange) files provide a global ionosphere delay estimation in a grid forma (in one or multiple layers) during one day. Optionally, it can also provide a sigma of the estimation in the same format. They are computed in postprocess by several agencies or universities, and are several times more accurate than Klobuchar.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SBAS:&lt;/b&gt; SBAS ionosphere model are computed and broadcasted in real time through the SBAS GEOs (messages type 18 and 26) in the area defined by the provider (e.g. Europe for EGNOS provider). Its accuracy is about to 1 metre.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;All ionosphere models can be applied to any constellation, and the  ionosphere effect can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;50 m&lt;/font&gt;  in turbulent ionospheric environments.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Ionospheric Correction</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="1" column="1" alignment="Qt::AlignLeft">
                           <widget class="QFrame" name="frameTropoCorrection">
                            <property name="frameShape">
                             <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                            </property>
                            <property name="frameShadow">
                             <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_85">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="verticalSpacing">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0" alignment="Qt::AlignLeft">
                              <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxTropoCorrection">
                               <property name="minimumSize">
                                <size>
                                 <width>125</width>
                                 <height>0</height>
                                </size>
                               </property>
                               <property name="font">
                                <font>
                                 <weight>50</weight>
                                 <bold>false</bold>
                                </font>
                               </property>
                               <property name="focusPolicy">
                                <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Tropospheric Nominal&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Two different tropospheric nominals are already implemented in gLAB :&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt; Simple Nominal &lt;/b&gt;: This approach allows a huge simplification of the model for the vertical delays because it does not require any surface meteorological data. Nominal values are computed as follows: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; = 2.3 · exp(−0.116 · 10&lt;sup&gt;−3&lt;/sup&gt; · H) &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; = 0.1&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; Where &lt;b&gt; H &lt;/b&gt; is the receiver height over the ellipsoid. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;br&gt; &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; UNB-3 Nominal&lt;/b&gt;: Where T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; and T&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; are calculated from the receiver’s height and estimates of five meteorological parameters: pressure [P (mbar)], temperature [T (K)], water vapour pressure [e (mbar)], temperature ”lapse” rate [β (o K/m)] and water vapour ”lapse rate” [λ (dimensionless)] according to procedure described in [RTCA-MOPS, 2006]. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                               </property>
                               <item>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>UNB-3 Nominal</string>
                                </property>
                               </item>
                               <item>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>Simple Nominal</string>
                                </property>
                               </item>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                             <item row="0" column="1" alignment="Qt::AlignLeft">
                              <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxTropoCorrectionMapping">
                               <property name="minimumSize">
                                <size>
                                 <width>127</width>
                                 <height>0</height>
                                </size>
                               </property>
                               <property name="font">
                                <font>
                                 <weight>50</weight>
                                 <bold>false</bold>
                                </font>
                               </property>
                               <property name="focusPolicy">
                                <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Tropospheric Mappings&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Two different tropospheric mappings are already implemented in gLAB :&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; &lt;b&gt; Simple Mapping &lt;/b&gt;:  It uses a common mapping for both components:&lt;br&gt; &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;  M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) = M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) =  M ( elev ) = 1.001 / sqrt ( 0.002001 + sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;( elev) ) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;The obliquity factor M ( elev ) is described in [Black and Eisner, 1984]. It is valid for satellite elevation angles over 5 degrees. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;br&gt; &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Niell Mapping &lt;/b&gt;: It does not require surface meteorology measurements, but provides comparable accuracy and precision to others that requires such data is presented in [Niell, 1996]. This mapping only use the receiver geographic location and measurement time as inputs. Niell’s mapping involves two different obliquity factors, for the M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;dry&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) and M&lt;i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;wet&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt;( elev ) components. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;br&gt;</string>
                               </property>
                               <item>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>Simple Mapping</string>
                                </property>
                               </item>
                               <item>
                                <property name="text">
                                 <string>Niell Mapping</string>
                                </property>
                               </item>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="1">
