                       </item>
                       <item row="0" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxSatClockOffset">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Satellite Clock Offset Correction&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The satellite clock offsets correspond to the clock synchronism errors of the satellite clocks in relation to the GNSS system time scale. These errors depend heavily on the type of oscillator of the satellite and are quite unpredictable. They can only be obtained by some kind of estimation. The typical source for estimations of these errors are the  &lt;b&gt;navigation messages&lt;/b&gt;, or some kind of external estimation, such as &lt;b&gt;SP3&lt;/b&gt; files. The effect of these clock offsets can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;hundreds of kilometres&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Satellite Clock Offset Correction</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="7" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxAntennaPhase">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Receiver antenna phase centre correction&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Normally the positions of the stations are given in relation to the base of the station. The difference between this point and the antenna phase centre should be taken into account. This effect depends on the frequency, and can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;some decimetres&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Receiver Antenna Phase Centre Correction</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="2" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxSatMovement">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Consider satellite movement during signal flight time&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Due to the distance between satellites and receivers (between 20000 and 30000 Km for GPS), the signal travel time is not despicable (about 70 ms for GPS). Thence the receiver is obtaining the measurement after it has been emitted by the satellite. This fact should be taken into consideration, as the position of the satellite must be computed in the transmission time, not in the reception time. This effect can impact on the measurements up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;hundreds of metres&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Consider Satellite Movement During Signal Flight Time</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="4" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxEarthRotation">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Consider Earth rotation during signal flight time&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Besides the satellite movement during signal flight time, the Earth also moves [rotates]. If this effect is not taken into consideration, an error of about &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;30 m&lt;/font&gt; in the east direction would be seen.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Consider Earth Rotation During Signal Flight Time</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="5" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxSatMassCentre">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Satellite Mass Centre to Antenna Phase Centre Offset Correction&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each data source of satellite orbits (in general the &lt;b&gt;navigation message&lt;/b&gt; or an &lt;b&gt;SP3&lt;/b&gt; file) provides these orbits in its specific reference. In particular, the &lt;b&gt;SP3&lt;/b&gt; files provide the positions of the satellite referred to its mass centre (which is different than the antenna phase centres). In order to properly correct the GNSS measurements with the satellite position, a correction between these two centres must be done. The positions extracted from the &lt;b&gt;navigation message&lt;/b&gt; do not require any additional corrections, as they are referred to the antenna phase centre.&lt;br&gt;Usually these corrections can be obtained from an ANTEX file.&lt;br&gt;This error can be up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;1-2 m&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;See description of ANTEX files in:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;File formats description&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Satellite Mass Centre to Antenna Phase Centre Offset Correction</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="8" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxAntennaReference">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Antenna Reference Point Correction&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Additionally to the Antenna Phase Centre, the position of a station can be given in relation to a specific point (such as a geodetically positioned point in the ground). This correction allows to give a specific correction to the position in North/East/Up components.&lt;br&gt;In most receivers, this correction is zero, but when it is not zero, its typical value is between &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;1-5 metres&lt;/font&gt;, especially in the Up component.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Receiver Antenna Reference Point Correction</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="12" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxWindUp">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Wind up correction&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The wind up only appears in carrier phase measurements and is due to the rotation of the Line-of-sight vector in relation to the antenna. The wind-up has an accumulative effect, and for fixed antennas can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;half the wave length&lt;/font&gt; of the measurement.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Wind up Correction (carrier phase only)</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="10" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxRelativisticClock">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Relativistic clock correction (orbit eccentricity)&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The rate of advance of two identical clocks, one placed in the satellite and the other on the terrestrial surface, will differ due to the difference of the gravitational potential (general relativity) and to the relative speed between them (special relativity). The special relativity difference can be broken into:&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A constant component that only depends on the nominal value of the semi-major axis of the satellite orbit, which is adjusted modifying the clock oscillating frequency of the satellite&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A periodical component due to the orbit eccentricity (that must be adjusted by the user receiver) equal to:&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;rel&lt;/i&gt; = 2*(&lt;b&gt;r&lt;/b&gt;·&lt;b&gt;v&lt;/b&gt;)/c&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;This effect can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;13 m&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Relativistic Clock Correction (orbit eccentricity)</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="13" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxTides">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Solid tides correction&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The attraction of Sun and Moon and the an-elasticity of the Earth's mantle causes variations to the positions of ground receivers. This effect can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;some decimetres&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Solid Tides Correction</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="14" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxRelativisticPath">
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <weight>50</weight>
                           <bold>false</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Relativistic path range correction&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As introduced in the &lt;i&gt;Relativistic clock correction&lt;/i&gt; section, the difference of the gravitational potential (general relativity) affects the measurement. This is a small effect that has an elevation dependence, and has a total effect of about &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;4 cm&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Relativistic Path Range Correction</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="1" column="0">
                        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxCheckBroadcastTransmissionTime">
                         <property name="toolTip">
                          <string>&lt;b&gt;Check Broadcast Transmission Time&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each RINEX navigation message has a transmission time field in it, which refers to the first time that the satellite sends the current navigation message, but receivers set it to the first time they receive the message. Therefore, receivers on different locations will set different transmission times in their RINEX navigation files, as satellite visibility will be different.&lt;br&gt;gLAB uses this time to check whether it can use or not use a navigation message, as if current epoch is previous to the transmission time, this means that the package was not available yet.&lt;br&gt;In SBAS and DGNSS this check is disabled, as in these modes corrections sent to the user are referred to a navigation message (with the IOD (Issue of Data)), therefore these navigation message had to be already sent by the satellite in order to compute the corrections.&lt;br&gt;See description of RINEX navigation files in:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;File formats description&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="text">
                          <string>Check Broadcast Transmission Time</string>
                         </property>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="6" column="0">
                        <widget class="QFrame" name="frameSatellitePhaseCenterVariation">
                         <property name="frameShape">
                          <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="frameShadow">
                          <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                         </property>
                         <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_356">
                          <property name="leftMargin">
                           <number>15</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="topMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="rightMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="bottomMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="spacing">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <item row="0" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxSatelliteAntennaPhaseCentreVariation">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Satellite Antenna Phase Centre Variation&lt;font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Satellite Mass Centre to Antenna Phase Centre Offset Correction has an additional term which is dependent on the satellite elevation. This additional term is also provided in the ANTEX file, on the next line after the Antenna Phase Centre Offset Correction.&lt;br&gt;This correction can be up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;1-5 cm.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;See description of ANTEX files in:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;File formats description&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Satellite Antenna Phase Centre Variation</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                         </layout>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                      </layout>
                     </widget>
                    </item>
                    <item row="2" column="0">
                     <spacer name="verticalSpacer_45">
                      <property name="orientation">
                       <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
                      </property>
                      <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                       <size>
                        <width>20</width>
                        <height>0</height>
                       </size>
                      </property>
                     </spacer>
                    </item>
                    <item row="1" column="0">
                     <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxShowDCBOptions">
                      <property name="font">
                       <font>
                        <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                        <weight>75</weight>
                        <bold>true</bold>
                       </font>
                      </property>
                      <property name="styleSheet">
                       <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                      </property>
                      <property name="title">
                       <string>Show DCB Options</string>
                      </property>
                      <property name="checkable">
                       <bool>true</bool>
                      </property>
                      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_412">
                       <item row="0" column="0">
                        <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptions">
                         <property name="frameShape">
                          <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="frameShadow">
                          <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                         </property>
                         <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_420">
                          <property name="leftMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="topMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="rightMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="bottomMargin">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="spacing">
                           <number>0</number>
                          </property>
                          <item row="1" column="0">
                           <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxShowDCBOptionsGalileo">
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                              <weight>75</weight>
                              <bold>true</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="title">
                             <string>Show Galileo</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checkable">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_414">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>9</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptionsGalileo">
                               <property name="frameShape">
                                <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="frameShadow">
                                <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_422">
                                <property name="leftMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="topMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="rightMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="bottomMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <item row="2" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfE1E5bGalileo">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="currentIndex">
                                   <number>0</number>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="2" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_524">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;Galileo DCB: E1 (F1) - E5b (F7)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For Galileo, broadcast orbits use two different iono-free (IF) combinations:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;I/NAV navigation message:&lt;/b&gt; Uses E1 and E5b (F7) iono-free combination. The exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F/NAV navigation message:&lt;/b&gt; Uses E1 and E5a (F5) iono-free combination. The exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on E1-E5a (F5) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX), but the exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-, but in Galileo they are named BGD -Broadcast Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of Galileo E1 (F1) - E5b (7) DCB (or BGD or TGD) provided in I/NAV navigation message, it corrects the bias between the single measurement in E1 and E5b to the reference IF combination of E1 and E5b. As the exact measurements attributes are not specified, gLAB assumes it can be applied to all measurements in E1 (C1A, C1B, C1C, C1X, C1Z) and E5b (C7I, C7Q and C7X).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This DCB (or BGD or TGD) is provided in the RINEX Navigation file, where the Galileo  E1 (F1) - E5b (F7) bias is given as the Broadcast Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;BGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the I/NAV broadcast ephemerides.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: E1 (F1) - E5b (F7)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_67">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;Galileo DCB: E1 (F1) - E5a (F5)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For Galileo, broadcast orbits use two different iono-free (IF) combinations:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;I/NAV navigation message:&lt;/b&gt; Uses E1 and E5b (F7) iono-free combination. The exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F/NAV navigation message:&lt;/b&gt; Uses E1 and E5a (F5) iono-free combination. The exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on E1-E5a (F5) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX), but the exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-, or in Galileo BGD -Broadcast Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of Galileo E1 (F1) - E5a (F5) DCB (or BGD or TGD) provided in F/NAV navigation message, it corrects the bias between the single measurement in E5a to the reference IF combination of E1 and E5a. As the exact measurements attributes are not specified, gLAB assumes it can be applied to all measurements in E5a (C5I, C5Q and C5X).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This DCB (or BGD or TGD) is provided in the RINEX Navigation file, where the Galileo E1 (F1) - E5a (F5) bias is given as the Broadcast Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;BGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the F/NAV broadcast ephemerides.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: E1 (F1) - E5a (F5)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfE1E5aGalileo">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="2">
