                          <item row="2" column="0">
                           <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxShowDCBOptionsGLONASS">
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                              <weight>75</weight>
                              <bold>true</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="title">
                             <string>Show GLONASS</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checkable">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_415">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>9</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptionsGLONASS">
                               <property name="frameShape">
                                <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="frameShadow">
                                <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_423">
                                <property name="leftMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="topMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="rightMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="bottomMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <item row="1" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_526">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GLONASS DCB: P1 - P2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GLONASS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1P and C2P is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of GLONASS P1-P2, it corrects the bias between the single measurement P1 or P2 to the reference IF combination of P1 and P2. This DCB (or TGD) is provided in the following files:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;Precise .DCB&lt;/b&gt; file, where the International GNSS Service (&lt;b&gt;IGS&lt;/b&gt;) gives an accurate estimation of the (P1-P2) bias. This file contains a monthly estimation of the (P1-P2) Differential Code Bias (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) for all Satellites. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;IONEX&lt;/b&gt; file, where a daily estimation of the (P2-P1) bias are given in the &lt;b&gt;PRN / BIAS / RMS&lt;/b&gt; header lines.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; Note that the GLONASS navigation message does not provide this DCB, therefore a user without external data providers cannot correct this DCB.&lt;br&gt;The GLONASS P1-P2 DCB is cancelled in the ionospheric-free combination. This effect can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;the meter level&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: P1 - P2</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfP1P2GLONASS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="currentIndex">
                                   <number>0</number>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>DCB File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>IONEX File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="2">
                                 <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_106">
                                  <property name="orientation">
                                   <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>234</width>
                                    <height>20</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                 </spacer>
                                </item>
                               </layout>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="3" column="0">
                           <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxShowDCBOptionsBDS">
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                              <weight>75</weight>
                              <bold>true</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="title">
                             <string>Show BDS</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checkable">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_417">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>9</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptionsBDS">
                               <property name="frameShape">
                                <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="frameShadow">
                                <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_424">
                                <property name="leftMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="topMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="rightMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="bottomMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <item row="0" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_68">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;BeiDou-2 DCB: B1 (F2) - B3 (F6)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For BeiDou (2 and 3), it is used the single frequency measurement B3i (C6I). In precise orbits and clocks, for BeiDou-2 it is used the IF based on B1 (F2) and B2 (F7) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX), but the exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified. For BeiDou-3, it is used the IF based on B1 (F2) and B3 (F6) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of BeiDou-2 B1 (F2) - B3 (F6) DCB (or TGD) provided in both D1 and D2 navigation messages, it corrects the bias between the single measurement in B1 to the reference single measurement B3I (C6I). As the exact measurements attributes are not specified, gLAB assumes it can be applied to all measurements in B1 (C2I, C2Q and C2X).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This DCB (or TGD) is provided in the RINEX Navigation file, where the Beidou-2 B1 (F2) - B3 (F6) bias is given as the Total Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;TGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the D1 or D2 broadcast ephemerides.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: B1 (F2) - B3 (F6)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="0" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfB2B6BDS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_528">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;BeiDou-2 DCB: B2b (F7) - B3 (F6)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For BeiDou (2 and 3), it is used the single frequency measurement B3i (C6I). In precise orbits and clocks, for BeiDou-2 it is used the IF based on B1 (F2) and B2 (F7) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX), but the exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified. For BeiDou-3, it is used the IF based on B1 (F2) and B3 (F6) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of BeiDou-2 B2b (F7) - B3 (F6) DCB (or TGD) provided in both D1 and D2 navigation messages, it corrects the bias between the single measurement in B1 to the reference single measurement B3I (C6I). As the exact measurements attributes are not specified, gLAB assumes it can be applied to all measurements in B1 (C2I, C2Q and C2X).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This DCB (or TGD) is provided in the RINEX Navigation file, where the Beidou-2 B2b (F7) - B3 (F6) bias is given as the Total Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;TGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 4&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the D1 or D2 broadcast ephemerides.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: B2b (F7) - B3 (F6)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfB7B6BDS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="2">
                                 <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_109">
                                  <property name="orientation">
                                   <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>0</width>
                                    <height>20</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                 </spacer>
                                </item>
                                <item row="2" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_527">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;BeiDou-2 DCB for SP3/CLK&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;BeiDou is the only constellation whose broadcast orbits and clocks use a single frequency measurement (B3I) as the reference. This creates a difference with respect the precise orbit and clock products, which use a dual frequency measurement as reference (usually the same as in broadcast orbits).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When the broadcast orbits and clocks have the same reference as the precise orbits and clocks, the DCBs provided in the navigation messages can be used with both broadcast and precise orbits and clocks. As this is not the case of BeiDou, it is required to apply the following formulas to account for the different reference signals:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;DCB to apply for single frequency B1 (F2) measurements:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;SP3 B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt; = c · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt; - c · (f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt; - f6&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt;) / (f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - f6&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;DCB to apply for single frequency B2b (F7) measurements:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;SP3 B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt; = c · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt; - c · (f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt; - f6&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt;) / (f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - f6&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; DCB between B1 (F2) - B3 (F6), as explained in tooltip &lt;i&gt;BeiDou -2 DCB: B1 (F2) - B3 (F6)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; DCB between B2b (F7) - B3 (F6), as explained in tooltip &lt;i&gt;BeiDou -2 DCB: B2b (F7) - B3 (F6)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f2:&lt;/b&gt; Frequency of B1 (F2) signal (1561.098 MHz)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f6:&lt;/b&gt; Frequency of B3 (F6) signal (1268.52 MHz)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;c:&lt;/b&gt; Speed of light&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB for SP3/CLK</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="2" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfSP3BDS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="3" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_75">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;Beidou DCB for Double Frequency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For BeiDou (2 and 3), it is used the single frequency measurement B3i (C6I). In precise orbits and clocks, for BeiDou-2 it is used the IF based on B1 (F2) and B2 (F7) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX), but the exact measurements attributes used to compute the IF are not specified. For BeiDou-3, it is used the IF based on B1 (F2) and B3 (F6) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;Prior to the introduction of new frequencies and signals in GPS, GLONASS and the introduction of new constellations, when working with dual frequency combinations, the DCBs could be applied correct the measurement either to each single frequency signal (that is, before computing the dual frequency combination) or after computing the dual frequency combination (with the adequate conversion factor).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With the introduction of new signals and frequencies, most of the dual frequency combinations do not match with the reference iono-free combination used to compute the orbits and clocks. In order to compute the adequate DCB correction, the ICD provides specific formulas which require some of the terms to be applied &lt;b&gt;after&lt;/b&gt; computing the dual frequency combination. As gLAB used to apply the DCB terms before the iono-free computation, and print each DCB term applied in a single frequency measurement in the MODEL message, it was decided to print the computed DCB from the ICD formula in a different term, named &quot;Double Frequency DCB&quot; in order to have a clear separation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In BeiDou-2, &lt;b&gt;for broadcast orbits only&lt;/b&gt; (see tooltip &lt;i&gt;DCB for SP3/CLK&lt;/i&gt;) the formulas for the DCBs are the following:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;B1 (F2) and B3 (F6):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Dual Frequency DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt; = (c · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;26&lt;/sub&gt; ) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;26&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;B2b (F7) and B3 (F6)&lt;/b&gt; (this combination is not in the ICD, but is analogous as the previous one):&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Dual Frequency DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt; = (c · DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;76&lt;/sub&gt; ) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;76&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;sub&gt;B1-B3&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; DCB explained in tooltip &lt;i&gt;DCB: B1 (F2) - B3 (F6)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;sub&gt;B2b-B3&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; DCB explained in tooltip &lt;i&gt;DCB: B2b (F7) - B3 (F6)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;c:&lt;/b&gt; Speed of light&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;26&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;/b&gt;  (f&lt;sub&gt;B1&lt;/sub&gt;/f&lt;sub&gt;B3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = (1561.098/1268.52)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;76&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;/b&gt;  (f&lt;sub&gt;B2B&lt;/sub&gt;/f&lt;sub&gt;B3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = (1207.14/1268.52)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; As the ICD does not specify the measurment attributes from B1 and B2b, gLAB will apply the formulas to all signals (C2I, C2Q, C2X for B1 and C7I, C7Q and C7X for B2B).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB for Double Frequency</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="3" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBdfBDS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
