                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                               </layout>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="0">
                           <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxShowDCBOptionsGPS">
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                              <weight>75</weight>
                              <bold>true</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="title">
                             <string>Show GPS</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checkable">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_413">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>9</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="spacing">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptionsGPS">
                               <property name="frameShape">
                                <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="frameShadow">
                                <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_421">
                                <property name="leftMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="topMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="rightMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="bottomMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <item row="2" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_162">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GPS DCB: P1 - P2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GPS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). As these signals are military encrypted, civil receivers report these measurements as C1W and C2W, as the tracking does not unencrypt the military signals. In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1W and C2W is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of GPS P1-P2, it corrects the bias between the single measurement P1 or P2 to the reference IF combination of P1 and P2. This DCB (or TGD) is provided in the following files:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;RINEX Navigation&lt;/b&gt; file, where the GPS (P2-P1) bias are given as the Total Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;TGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides (LNAV and CNAV navigation messages). This estimation is generated by the Control Segment that monitorises all satellites.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;Precise .DCB&lt;/b&gt; file, where the International GNSS Service (&lt;b&gt;IGS&lt;/b&gt;) gives an accurate estimation of the (P1-P2) bias. This file contains a monthly estimation of the (P1-P2) Differential Code Bias (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) for all Satellites. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;IONEX&lt;/b&gt; file, where a daily estimation of the (P2-P1) bias are given in the &lt;b&gt;PRN / BIAS / RMS&lt;/b&gt; header lines.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The GPS P1-P2 DCB is cancelled in the ionospheric-free combination. This effect can reach up to &lt;font color=&quot;red&quot;&gt;the meter level&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;About TGDs &amp;amp; DCBs:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The relation between the DCBs of the precise files or IONEX DCBs and the TGDs broadcast in the GPS navigation message is:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;TGD&lt;sub&gt;GPS Broadcast Message&lt;/sub&gt; = -&amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt; / ( &amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt; ) · DCB&lt;sub&gt;File&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;TGD&lt;sub&gt;GPS Broadcast Message&lt;/sub&gt; = -&amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt; / ( &amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt; ) · IONEX&lt;sub&gt;DCB&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;alpha;&lt;sub&gt;i&lt;/sub&gt; = 40.3 / f&lt;sub&gt;i&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: P1 - P2</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="3" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_163">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GPS ISC: L1 C/A - L1 P(Y)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GPS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). As these signals are military encrypted, civil receivers report these measurements as C1W and C2W, as the tracking does not unencrypt the military signals. In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1W and C2W is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;ISC L1 C/A - L1 P(Y) is located in the 1&lt;sup&gt;st&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides CNAV navigation message and converts the bias from C1 to P1. As this ISC is the same as DCB: C1-P1, it can also be applied to get consistent measurements according to the GPS receiver type (see &lt;i&gt;DCB: C1 - P1&lt;/i&gt; tooltip for details).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; If option GPS DCB C1-P1 is set to strict and ISC L1 C/A - L1 P(Y) is enabled, DCB C1-P1 (from DCB file) will be used.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>ISC: L1 C/A - L1 P(Y)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfP1C1GPS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
