                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="4" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_164">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GPS ISC: L2C (M or L) - L1 P(Y)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GPS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). As these signals are military encrypted, civil receivers report these measurements as C1W and C2W, as the tracking does not unencrypt the military signals. In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1W and C2W is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;ISC L2C (M or L) - L1 P(Y) is located in the 2&lt;sup&gt;nd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides CNAV navigation message and converts the bias from C2S, C2L or C2X to C1P.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; C2X measurement is not specified in GPS ICD. gLAB will apply to C2X the same criteria as C2S or C2L as they all have the same reference signal according to RINEX standard.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>ISC: L2C (M or L) - L1 P(Y)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
