                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_66">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GPS DCB: C1 - P1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GPS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). As these signals are military encrypted, civil receivers report these measurements as C1W and C2W, as the tracking does not unencrypt the military signals. In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1W and C2W is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of GPS C1-P1, it is called DCB for historical reasons (as at that time the term &quot;ISC&quot; did not exist), but it is indeed an ISC, now provided in the CNAV message (ISC L1 C/A - L1 P(Y)). Before the CNAV broadcast navigation message, this ISC was only provided by CODE GPS P1-C1 files (containing the C1-P1 DCB but with the sign changed, therefore they are known as P1-C1 DCB files).&lt;br&gt;The GPS C1-P1 DCB (or ISC) converts the signal C1 to P1. This DCB is also a special case, as GPS receivers used C1 to track P1 and P2, therefore depending on the receiver type, it is also necessary to apply this DCB to get consistent P1 and P2 measurements:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 0 &lt;/b&gt;: GPS C1-P1 classification unknown, no correction applied. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 1 &lt;/b&gt;: Cross correlated receiver, reporting:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;C1&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;P2 = C1 + (Y&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; - Y&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;Needs Corrections to obtain P1 and a consistent P2: P1=C1+b and P2=P2+b&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Type 2 &lt;/b&gt;: C1 reported in place of P1:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;Needs Corrections to obtain P1: P1=C1+b&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Mark this option to correct GPS C1 - P1 bias. Because the GPS code generation depends on the GPS Receiver Type, this GPS receiver-related information has to be given together with the corrections.  gLAB works in two different modes:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flexible:&lt;/b&gt; gLAB will use whichever GPS C1 or P1 measurement is available in the receiver. If ISC L1 C/A - L1 P(Y) from CNAV is set and available, it will apply the ISC correction to C1 if it is used. Moreover, if a GPS Receiver type is provided, it will apply the ISC according to the receiver type. If ISC is not available, &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;C1-P1 DCB will not be corrected&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;. If both code measurements are available, P1 will be used as default. Used when receiver provides C1 but P1 is missing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; Strict:&lt;/b&gt; gLAB &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt; stops if the receiver cannot be matched &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;with the GPS Receiver Type File or &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color='#C00000'&gt;both&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; files are not provided (in the Input Section): &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; GPS P1-C1 DCB File: Containing the GPS P1-C1 DCB corrections.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; GPS Receiver Type File: To identify how codes are generated in the receiver, and how to remove these GPS P1-C1 biases.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; If option GPS DCB C1-P1 is set to strict and ISC L1 C/A - L1 P(Y) is enabled, DCB C1-P1 (from DCB file) will be used.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="autoFillBackground">
                                   <bool>false</bool>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: C1 - P1</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="6" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_166">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GPS ISC: L5Q5 - L1 P(Y)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GPS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). As these signals are military encrypted, civil receivers report these measurements as C1W and C2W, as the tracking does not unencrypt the military signals. In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1W and C2W is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;ISC L5Q5  - L1 P(Y) is located in the 4&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides CNAV navigation message and converts the bias from C5Q to C1P.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>ISC: L5Q5 - L1 P(Y)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="5" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxISCsfL5I5GPS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="7" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_74">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;GPS DCB for Double Frequency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For GPS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of measurements P1 and P2 (C1P and C2P in RINEX3 notation). As these signals are military encrypted, civil receivers report these measurements as C1W and C2W, as the tracking does not unencrypt the military signals. In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on C1W and C2W is used by most providers (e.g IGS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;Prior to the introduction of new frequencies and signals in GPS, GLONASS and the introduction of new constellations, when working with dual frequency combinations, the DCBs could be applied correct the measurement either to each single frequency signal (that is, before computing the dual frequency combination) or after computing the dual frequency combination (with the adequate conversion factor).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With the introduction of new signals and frequencies, most of the dual frequency combinations do not match with the reference iono-free combination used to compute the orbits and clocks. In order to compute the adequate DCB correction, the ICD provides specific formulas which require some of the terms to be applied &lt;b&gt;after&lt;/b&gt; computing the dual frequency combination. As gLAB used to apply the DCB terms before the iono-free computation, and print each DCB term applied in a single frequency measurement in the MODEL message, it was decided to print the computed DCB from the ICD formula in a different term, named &quot;Double Frequency DCB&quot; in order to have a clear separation. In GPS, the formulas for the DCBs are the following:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (C2S or C2L):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1 C/A (C1C) - L2C&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L2C&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1 C/A&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1 C/A (C1C) and L5I5 (C5I):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1C/A - L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1C/A&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1 C/A (C1C) and L5Q5 (C5Q):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1C/A - L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1C/A&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;P&lt;/sub&gt; (C1L) and L2C (C2S or C2L):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CP - L2C&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L2C&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CP&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; (C1S) and L2C (C2S or C2L):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CD - L2C&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L2C&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CD&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;P&lt;/sub&gt; (C1L) and L5Q5 (C5Q):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CP - L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CP&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; (C1S) and L5Q5 (C5Q):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CD - L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CD&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;P&lt;/sub&gt; (C1L) and L5I5 (C5I):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CP - L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CP&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; (C1S) and L5Q5 (C5I):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CD - L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CD&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;In SBAS DFMC, the ISC are already incorporated in the SBAS DFMC corrections, therefore the following formula is used:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1 C/A (C1C) and L5Q5 (C5Q):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;SBAS DFMC L1C/A - L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; = - c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;ISC&lt;sub&gt;i&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Inter-signal correction for the channel indicated by the subscript&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;  DCB correction explained in tooltip &lt;i&gt;GPS DCB: P1-P2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;c:&lt;/b&gt; Speed of light&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;/b&gt;  (f&lt;sub&gt;L1&lt;/sub&gt;/f&lt;sub&gt;L2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = (77/60)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;/b&gt;  (f&lt;sub&gt;L1&lt;/sub&gt;/f&lt;sub&gt;L5&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = (154/115)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; C1X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C1X the same criteria as C1S or C1L as they all have the same reference signal according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; C2X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C2X the same criteria as C2S or C2L as they all have the same reference signal according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;C5X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C5X the same criteria as C5X has the same reference signal as C5I according to RINEX standard.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB for Double Frequency</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="7" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBdfGPS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                               </layout>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="0">
                           <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxShowDCBOptionsQZSS">
                            <property name="font">
                             <font>
                              <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                              <weight>75</weight>
                              <bold>true</bold>
                             </font>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="title">
                             <string>Show QZSS</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checkable">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_418">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>9</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptionsQZSS">
                               <property name="frameShape">
                                <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="frameShadow">
                                <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_425">
                                <property name="leftMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="topMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="rightMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="bottomMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <item row="0" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_532">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;QZSS: DCB: Clock - L1 C/A (C1C)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For QZSS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes). In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of QZSS Clock - L1 C/A (C1C), it corrects the bias between the single measurement C1C to the reference IF combination of L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C. This DCB (or TGD) is provided in the RINEX Navigation file, where the QZSS Clock - L1 C/A (C1C) bias is given as the Total Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;TGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides (LNAV and CNAV navigation messages).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; In case of using L1 C/B (C1E), the same criteria will apply as in L1 C/A (C1C).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: Clock - L1 C/A</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="0" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfC1CQZSS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_531">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;QZSS ISC: L1 C/A - L2C (M or L)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For QZSS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes). In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;ISC L1 C/A - L2C (M or L) is located in the 2&lt;sup&gt;nd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides CNAV navigation message and converts the bias from C2S or C2L to C1C.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; C2X measurement is not specified in QZSS ICD. gLAB will apply to C2X the same criteria as C2S or C2L as they all have the same reference signal according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; In case of using L1 C/B (C1E), the same criteria will apply as in L1 C/A.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>ISC: L1 C/A - L2C (M or L)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxISCsfL2CQZSS">
