                                </item>
                                <item row="2" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_534">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;QZSS ISC: L1 C/A - L5I5&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For QZSS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes). In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;ISC L1 C/A - L5I5 is located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides CNAV navigation message and converts the bias from C5I to C1C.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; C5X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C5X the same criteria as C5X has the same reference signal as C5I according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; In case of using L1 C/B (C1E), the same criteria will apply as in L1 C/A.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>ISC: L1 C/A - L5I5</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="2" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxISCsfL5I5QZSS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>RINEX Nav File</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="3" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_530">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;QZSS ISC: L1 C/A - L5Q5&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For QZSS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes). In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;ISC L1 C/A - L5Q5 is located in the 4&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides CNAV navigation message and converts the bias from C5Q to C1C.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; In case of using L1 C/B (C1E), the same criteria will apply as in L1 C/A.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>ISC: L1 C/A - L5Q5</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="3" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxISCsfL5Q5QZSS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
                                   <property name="text">
                                    <string>No</string>
                                   </property>
                                  </item>
