                                   </property>
                                  </item>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="4" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_161">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;QZSS DCB for Double Frequency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For QZSS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes). In precise orbits and clocks, the IF based on L1 C/A (C1C) and L2C (for L2C it is not specified the exact measurement attributes) is used by most providers (e.g MGEX).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;Prior to the introduction of new frequencies and signals in GPS, GLONASS and the introduction of new constellations, when working with dual frequency combinations, the DCBs could be applied correct the measurement either to each single frequency signal (that is, before computing the dual frequency combination) or after computing the dual frequency combination (with the adequate conversion factor).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With the introduction of new signals and frequencies, most of the dual frequency combinations do not match with the reference iono-free combination used to compute the orbits and clocks. In order to compute the adequate DCB correction, the ICD provides specific formulas which require some of the terms to be applied &lt;b&gt;after&lt;/b&gt; computing the dual frequency combination. As gLAB used to apply the DCB terms before the iono-free computation, and print each DCB term applied in a single frequency measurement in the MODEL message, it was decided to print the computed DCB from the ICD formula in a different term, named &quot;Double Frequency DCB&quot; in order to have a clear separation. In QZSS, the formulas for the DCBs are the following:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;P&lt;/sub&gt; (C1L) and L2C (C2S or C2L):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CP - L2C&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L2C&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CP&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;) + c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; (C1S) and L2C (C2S or C2L):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CD - L2C&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L2C&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CD&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;) + c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;P&lt;/sub&gt; (C1L) and L5Q5 (C5Q):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CP - L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CP&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) + c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; (C1S) and L5Q5 (C5Q):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CD - L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5Q5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CD&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) + c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;P&lt;/sub&gt; (C1L) and L5I5 (C5I):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CP - L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CP&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) + c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L1C&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; (C1S) and L5Q5 (C5I):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DCB&lt;sub&gt;L1CD - L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; = c · (ISC&lt;sub&gt;L5I5&lt;/sub&gt; - &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; · ISC&lt;sub&gt;L1CD&lt;/sub&gt;) / (1- &amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;) + c · T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;ISC&lt;sub&gt;i&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Inter-signal correction for the channel indicated by the subscript&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;T&lt;sub&gt;GD&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;  DCB correction explained in tooltip &lt;i&gt;QZSS DCB: Clock - L1 C/A&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;c:&lt;/b&gt; Speed of light&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;/b&gt;  (f&lt;sub&gt;L1&lt;/sub&gt;/f&lt;sub&gt;L2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = (77/60)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;gamma;&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;/b&gt;  (f&lt;sub&gt;L1&lt;/sub&gt;/f&lt;sub&gt;L5&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = (154/115)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; C1X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C1X the same criteria as C1S or C1L as they all have the same reference signal according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; C2X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C2X the same criteria as C2S or C2L as they all have the same reference signal according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;C5X is not specified in the ICD, but gLAB will apply to C5X the same criteria as C5X has the same reference signal as C5I according to RINEX standard.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; In case of using L1 C/B (C1E), the same criteria will apply as in L1 C/A.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB for Double Frequency</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="4" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBdfQZSS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="focusPolicy">
                                   <enum>Qt::StrongFocus</enum>
                                  </property>
                                  <item>
