                              <number>6</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QFrame" name="frameShowDCBOptionsIRNSS">
                               <property name="frameShape">
                                <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                               </property>
                               <property name="frameShadow">
                                <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_426">
                                <property name="leftMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="topMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="rightMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <property name="bottomMargin">
                                 <number>6</number>
                                </property>
                                <item row="1" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_72">
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;IRNSS: DCB: S-SPS (C9A) - L5-SPS (C5A)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Differential Code Biases (&lt;b&gt;DCB&lt;/b&gt;) are the delays due to electronic, antennas and cables of receiver and transmitter devices which directly affect the measurements with a bias.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When satellite orbits and clocks are estimated, a reference measurement or combination must be selected. For IRNSS, broadcast orbits use the iono-free (IF) combination of S (F9) and L5 frequencies, but the exact reference measurements attributes are not specified (assumed C9A and C5A). Precise orbits and clocks are currently not provided for this constellation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reference measurement or combination, by definition, always has all satellite DCB=0. Therefore, when a user utilizes any measurement (or combination) which is different from the reference combination, a bias appears in the clock estimate, which is what the DCB corrects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DCB correction can be provided in two ways:&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Directly correcting the DCB for one specific measurement (note that DCB are always referred to a single measurement) to the reference measurement or combination (they are usually named DCB or TGD -Total Group Delay-)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Providing a correction that converts (i.e. adjust the bias) a measurement to another measurement which has a DCB that corrects the remaining bias (therefore multiple corrections will have to be applied to fully remove the bias). These are refered as Inter Signal Correction (ISC).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;In the case of IRNSS S-SPS (C9) - L5-SPS (C5), it corrects the bias between the single measurement C9A and C5A to the reference IF combination of S (F9) and L5. It is assumed the reference measurements are C9A and C5A as these are the ones for SPS (Standard Positioning Service) and are also the reference signals specified in the RINEX standard. This DCB (or TGD) is provided in the RINEX Navigation file, where the IRNSS (C9A-C5A) bias is given as the Total Group Delay (&lt;b&gt;TGD&lt;/b&gt;) located in the 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; field of the 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; row of the broadcast ephemerides (LNAV navigation message). This estimation is generated by the Control Segment that monitorises all satellites.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>DCB: S-SPS (C9A) - L5-SPS (C5A)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="1" column="1">
                                 <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBoxDCBsfC9C5IRNSS">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>120</width>
                                    <height>0</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
