                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
                                        <item row="0" column="0">
                                         <widget class="QLabel" name="label_777">
                                          <property name="maximumSize">
                                           <size>
                                            <width>16777215</width>
                                            <height>22</height>
                                           </size>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="font">
                                           <font>
                                            <weight>50</weight>
                                            <bold>false</bold>
                                           </font>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="toolTip">
                                           <string>&lt;b&gt;Smoothing with:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the combination type to smooth the third Galileo code measurement. The possible combinations are:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Auto:&lt;/b&gt; gLAB will automatically select the same combination type as the code measurement (single frequency carrier phase for single frequency code measurement and carrier phase ionosphere-free combination for code ionosphere-free combination respectively) for smoothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SF:&lt;/b&gt; Use a Single Frequency (SF) carrier phase for smoothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;GC:&lt;/b&gt; Use a Graphic Combination (GC) for smoothing. This combination removes the ionosphere and has the pseudorange code noise halved. It is obtained with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;GC = (&lt;i&gt;Pseudorange&lt;/i&gt; + &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase&lt;/i&gt;)/2&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;IF:&lt;/b&gt; Use a carrier phase Ionosphere-Free (IF) combination for smoothing. It is computed with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;IF = (f1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase1&lt;/i&gt; -  f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase2&lt;/i&gt;)/(f1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The frequency of the first carrier phase.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;  The frequency of the second carrier phase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;DF:&lt;/b&gt; Use a Divergence Free (DF) dual frequency combination for smoothing. This combination has no ionospheric divergence (hence the name) that occurs when using single frequency smoothing (see &lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;https://gssc.esa.int/navipedia/index.php/Code-Carrier_Divergence_Effect&lt;/font&gt; for details). It is computed with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DF = &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase1&lt;/i&gt; +2 · f&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;/(f&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt; - f&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;) · (&lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase1&lt;/i&gt; - &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase2&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The frequency of the first carrier phase.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The frequency of the second carrier phase.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="styleSheet">
                                           <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="text">
                                           <string>Smoothing with:</string>
                                          </property>
                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
                                        <item row="0" column="3">
                                         <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_262">
                                          <property name="orientation">
                                           <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                           <size>
                                            <width>0</width>
                                            <height>20</height>
                                           </size>
                                          </property>
                                         </spacer>
                                        </item>
                                       </layout>
                                      </widget>
                                     </item>
                                     <item row="2" column="0">
                                      <widget class="QFrame" name="framePhaseGalileo_3">
                                       <property name="frameShape">
                                        <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="frameShadow">
                                        <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                                       </property>
                                       <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_974">
                                        <property name="leftMargin">
                                         <number>0</number>
                                        </property>
                                        <property name="topMargin">
                                         <number>0</number>
                                        </property>
                                        <property name="rightMargin">
                                         <number>0</number>
                                        </property>
                                        <property name="bottomMargin">
                                         <number>0</number>
                                        </property>
                                        <property name="horizontalSpacing">
                                         <number>3</number>
                                        </property>
                                        <property name="verticalSpacing">
                                         <number>0</number>
                                        </property>
                                        <item row="0" column="19">
                                         <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_192">
                                          <property name="orientation">
                                           <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                           <size>
                                            <width>0</width>
                                            <height>20</height>
                                           </size>
                                          </property>
                                         </spacer>
                                        </item>
                                        <item row="0" column="8">
                                         <widget class="QLabel" name="label_620">
                                          <property name="sizePolicy">
                                           <sizepolicy hsizetype="Fixed" vsizetype="Preferred">
                                            <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                                            <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                                           </sizepolicy>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="toolTip">
                                           <string>&lt;b&gt;StdDev:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the standard deviation mode for the third Galileo carrier phase measurement in the filter. There are five different modes:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fixed:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is a fixed constant:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma; = a (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is provided by the user (in metres).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.01 metres for single frequency and 0.03 metres for dual frequency combination.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Elevation:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on satellite's elevation using an exponential:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma; = a + b·e&lt;sup&gt;(-&amp;theta;/c)&lt;/sup&gt; (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; in degrees). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.01 metres for single frequency and 0.03 metres for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 0.53 metres and for &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; is 10 degrees. &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; default values are from MOPS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;sin(elevation):&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the inverse of the square of the satellite's elevation:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b/(sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;(&amp;theta;))  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1E-4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for single frequency and 9E-4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 2.5E-3 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SNR:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the satellite's SNR (Signal to Noise Ratio):&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b · 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; in  metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;·Hz). &lt;i&gt;SNR&lt;/i&gt; is the satellite's SNR (in dBHz).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1E-4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for single frequency and 9E-4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SNR + sin(elevation):&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the inverse of the square of the satellite's elevation and SNR:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b · 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;/(sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;(&amp;theta;))  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;·Hz). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees) and &lt;i&gt;SNR&lt;/i&gt; the satellite's SNR (in dBHz).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1E-4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for single frequency and 9E-4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In command line, the constant parameter &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; can be set (in all weight modes) to the text &lt;i&gt;URA&lt;/i&gt;. With this option, parameter &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is set to the URA (User Range Accuracy) provided in the navigation message (therefore, this option can only be used when a navigation message is used for satellite orbits).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For weights involving the SNR, in command line it is possible to control how the SNR measurement is computed for a combination (e.g using the SNR of a specific frequency, using the minimum or maximum SNR of all signals involved, using the mean SNR of all signals involved or weighting each signal SNR with a user defined ratio) using option '-filter:snrweight:comb'. The default method is to use mean SNR value of all signals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="styleSheet">
                                           <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="text">
                                           <string>StdDev:</string>
                                          </property>
                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
