                                            <item row="0" column="0">
                                             <widget class="QLabel" name="label_597">
                                              <property name="sizePolicy">
                                               <sizepolicy hsizetype="Fixed" vsizetype="Preferred">
                                                <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                                                <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                                               </sizepolicy>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="toolTip">
                                               <string>&lt;b&gt;StdDev:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the standard deviation mode for the first Galileo code measurement in the filter. There are five different modes:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fixed:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is a fixed constant:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma; = a (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is provided by the user (in metres).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1 metre for single frequency and 3 metres for dual frequency combination.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Elevation:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on satellite's elevation using an exponential:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma; = a + b·e&lt;sup&gt;(-&amp;theta;/c)&lt;/sup&gt; (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; in degrees). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1 metre for single frequency and 3 metres for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 0.53 metres and for &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; is 10 degrees. &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; default values are from MOPS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;sin(elevation):&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the inverse of the square of the satellite's elevation:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b/(sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;(&amp;theta;))  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1 metre&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for single frequency and 9 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 2.5E-3 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SNR:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the satellite's SNR (Signal to Noise Ratio):&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b · 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; in  metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;·Hz). &lt;i&gt;SNR&lt;/i&gt; is the satellite's SNR (in dBHz).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1 metre&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for single frequency and 9 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SNR + sin(elevation):&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the inverse of the square of the satellite's elevation and SNR:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b · 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;/(sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;(&amp;theta;))  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;·Hz). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees) and &lt;i&gt;SNR&lt;/i&gt; the satellite's SNR (in dBHz).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 1 metre&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for single frequency and 9 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for dual frequency combination, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In command line, the constant parameter &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; can be set (in all weight modes) to the text &lt;i&gt;URA&lt;/i&gt;. With this option, parameter &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is set to the URA (User Range Accuracy) provided in the navigation message (therefore, this option can only be used when a navigation message is used for satellite orbits).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For weights involving the SNR, in command line it is possible to control how the SNR measurement is computed for a combination (e.g using the SNR of a specific frequency, using the minimum or maximum SNR of all signals involved, using the mean SNR of all signals involved or weighting each signal SNR with a user defined ratio) using option '-filter:snrweight:comb'. The default method is to use mean SNR value of all signals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="styleSheet">
                                               <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="text">
                                               <string>StdDev:</string>
                                              </property>
                                             </widget>
                                            </item>
                                            <item row="0" column="6">
                                             <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_190">
                                              <property name="orientation">
                                               <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                               <size>
                                                <width>0</width>
                                                <height>20</height>
                                               </size>
                                              </property>
                                             </spacer>
                                            </item>
                                           </layout>
                                          </widget>
                                          <widget class="QWidget" name="pageStdDevGalileoSBAS_1">
                                           <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_947">
                                            <property name="leftMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="topMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="rightMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="bottomMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="horizontalSpacing">
                                             <number>3</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="verticalSpacing">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <item row="0" column="0">
                                             <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonStdDevCodeSBASGalileo_1">
                                              <property name="sizePolicy">
                                               <sizepolicy hsizetype="Fixed" vsizetype="Fixed">
                                                <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                                                <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                                               </sizepolicy>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="font">
                                               <font>
                                                <weight>50</weight>
                                                <bold>false</bold>
                                               </font>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="toolTip">
                                               <string>&lt;b&gt;StdDev from SBAS 1F messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In SBAS 1F mode, the standard deviation is computed using the messages from SBAS 1F. The standard deviation from SBAS 1F is obtained from the deviation of the fast and slow corrections, ionosphere, troposphere and the receiver model. The formula to obtain the standard deviation in SBAS 1F is:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;sat&lt;/sub&gt; = &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;flt&lt;/sub&gt; + &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;ionosphere&lt;/sub&gt; + &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;troposphere&lt;/sub&gt; + &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;air&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;flt&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance for fast and long term corrections. See &lt;i&gt;Degradation Parameters&lt;/i&gt;  in the MODELLING section for details on how to compute it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;ionosphere&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance of the ionosphere. When SBAS 1F iono messages are used, the variance is computed with an interpolation from the variance of the grid points used for computing the ionosphere delay (with an specific degradation term applied), or if Klobuchar model is used, a specific formula is utilized (see MOPS for details on how to compute the ionosphere variance).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;troposphere&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance of the troposphere (see MOPS for details on how to compute it).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;air&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance of the airborne receiver. See &lt;i&gt;Airborne Receiver Type&lt;/i&gt; in the MODELLING section for details on how to compute it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; In command line it is possible to override the default SBAS weight (i.e. use any of the gLAB available weight functions) or to add the SBAS weight to the weight computed with any of the gLAB available weight functions. Use option '-filter:sbasdgnssweightmode' to overrride the default SBAS weight and any of the options '-filter:fixedweight', '-filter:elevweight', ' -filter:sinelevweight', '-filter:snrweight' or '-filter:snrelevweight' to set the new weight function.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="styleSheet">
                                               <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="text">
                                               <string>StdDev from SBAS 1F messages</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="checked">
                                               <bool>true</bool>
                                              </property>
                                             </widget>
                                            </item>
                                            <item row="0" column="1">
                                             <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_191">
                                              <property name="orientation">
                                               <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                                               <size>
                                                <width>0</width>
                                                <height>20</height>
                                               </size>
                                              </property>
                                             </spacer>
                                            </item>
                                           </layout>
                                          </widget>
                                          <widget class="QWidget" name="pageStdDevGalileoSBASDFMC_1">
                                           <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_130">
                                            <property name="leftMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="topMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="rightMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="bottomMargin">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <property name="spacing">
                                             <number>0</number>
                                            </property>
                                            <item row="0" column="0">
                                             <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonradioButtonStdDevCodeSBASDFMCGalileo_1">
                                              <property name="toolTip">
                                               <string>&lt;b&gt;StdDev from SBAS DFMC messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In SBAS DFMC mode, the standard deviation is computed using the messages from SBAS DFMC. The standard deviation from SBAS DFMC is obtained from the DFRE (Dual Frequency Range Error) parameters, ionosphere residual, troposphere and the receiver model. The formula to obtain the standard deviation in SBAS DFMC is:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;sat&lt;/sub&gt; = &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;DFC&lt;/sub&gt; + &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;UIRE&lt;/sub&gt; + &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;troposphere&lt;/sub&gt; + &amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;air&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;DFC&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance for SBAS DFMC correction or DFC (Dual Frequency Corrections). See &lt;i&gt;Integrity Messages&lt;/i&gt;  in the MODELLING section for details on how to compute it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;UIRE&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance of the residual of the ionosphere.  See &lt;i&gt;Set Sigma UIRE Value&lt;/i&gt;  in the MODELLING section for details on how to compute it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;troposphere&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance of the troposphere (see MOPS for details on how to compute it).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;air&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Variance of the airborne receiver. See &lt;i&gt;Airborne Receiver Type&lt;/i&gt; in the MODELLING section for details on how to compute it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; In command line it is possible to override the default SBAS weight (i.e. use any of the gLAB available weight functions) or to add the SBAS weight to the weight computed with any of the gLAB available weight functions. Use option '-filter:sbasdgnssweightmode' to overrride the default SBAS weight and any of the options '-filter:fixedweight', '-filter:elevweight', ' -filter:sinelevweight', '-filter:snrweight' or '-filter:snrelevweight' to set the new weight function.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="styleSheet">
                                               <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="text">
                                               <string>StdDev from SBAS DFMC messages</string>
                                              </property>
                                              <property name="checked">
                                               <bool>true</bool>
                                              </property>
                                             </widget>
                                            </item>
                                            <item row="0" column="1">
                                             <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_97">
                                              <property name="orientation">
                                               <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                                              </property>
