                                        <item row="0" column="7">
                                         <widget class="QLabel" name="label_882">
                                          <property name="sizePolicy">
                                           <sizepolicy hsizetype="Fixed" vsizetype="Preferred">
                                            <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                                            <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                                           </sizepolicy>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="maximumSize">
                                           <size>
                                            <width>16777215</width>
                                            <height>22</height>
                                           </size>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="toolTip">
                                           <string>&lt;b&gt;StdDev:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the standard deviation mode for the first Galileo graphical combination (GC) in the filter. There are five different modes:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fixed:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is a fixed constant:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma; = a (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is provided by the user (in metres).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.5 metres.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Elevation:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on satellite's elevation using an exponential:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma; = a + b·e&lt;sup&gt;(-&amp;theta;/c)&lt;/sup&gt; (metres)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; in degrees). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.5 metres, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 0.53 metres and for &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; is 10 degrees. &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt; default values are from MOPS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;sin(elevation):&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the inverse of the square of the satellite's elevation:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b/(sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;(&amp;theta;))  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.25 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 2.5E-3 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SNR:&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the satellite's SNR (Signal to Noise Ratio):&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b · 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; in  metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;·Hz). &lt;i&gt;SNR&lt;/i&gt; is the satellite's SNR (in dBHz).&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.25 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SNR + sin(elevation):&lt;/b&gt; The standard deviation is dependent on the inverse of the square of the satellite's elevation and SNR:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;sigma;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; = a + b · 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;/(sin&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;(&amp;theta;))  (metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; are the values provided by the user (being &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; in metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;·Hz). &amp;theta; is the satellite's elevation (in degrees) and &lt;i&gt;SNR&lt;/i&gt; the satellite's SNR (in dBHz).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The default value for &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is 0.25 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;, for &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; is 4 metres&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt; value is chosen for having similar values as the MOPS exponential.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In command line, the constant parameter &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; can be set (in all weight modes) to the text &lt;i&gt;URA&lt;/i&gt;. With this option, parameter &lt;i&gt;a&lt;/i&gt; is set to the URA (User Range Accuracy) provided in the navigation message (therefore, this option can only be used when a navigation message is used for satellite orbits).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For weights involving the SNR, in command line it is possible to control how the SNR measurement is computed for a combination (e.g using the SNR of a specific frequency, using the minimum or maximum SNR of all signals involved, using the mean SNR of all signals involved or weighting each signal SNR with a user defined ratio) using option '-filter:snrweight:comb'. The default method is to use mean SNR value of all signals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="styleSheet">
                                           <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="text">
                                           <string>StdDev:</string>
                                          </property>
                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
