                                          </property>
                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
                                        <item row="0" column="0">
                                         <widget class="QLabel" name="labelPhaseBDS_1">
                                          <property name="toolTip">
                                           <string>&lt;b&gt;Phase Freq:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the frequency (for single frequency) or the two frequencies (for dual frequency combinations) for the first BDS carrier phase measurement in the filter. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; If it is set to &lt;i&gt;Auto&lt;/i&gt;, gLAB will automatically select them according to the frequency order (see option &lt;i&gt;Set GNSS Frequencies and Measurements Order&lt;/i&gt; above) and the available ones in the RINEX observation file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If there are multiple carrier phase frequencies (per constellation) set to &lt;i&gt;Auto&lt;/i&gt;, only one carrier phase measurement will be automatically selected by gLAB for the filter.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In dual frequency combinations, &lt;i&gt;PC&lt;/i&gt; is used for the code ionospheric-free combination, and &lt;i&gt;LC&lt;/i&gt; for the carrier phase ionospheric-free combination. This is to avoid confusion, as IF (Ionospheric-Free) can refer to both the code and carrier phase ionospheric-free combinations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="styleSheet">
                                           <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="text">
                                           <string>Phase Freq:</string>
                                          </property>
                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
