                                        </item>
                                        <item row="0" column="0">
                                         <widget class="QLabel" name="label_837">
                                          <property name="font">
                                           <font>
                                            <weight>50</weight>
                                            <bold>false</bold>
                                           </font>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="toolTip">
                                           <string>&lt;b&gt;Smoothing with:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the combination type to smooth the first QZSS code measurement. The possible combinations are:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Auto:&lt;/b&gt; gLAB will automatically select the same combination type as the code measurement (single frequency carrier phase for single frequency code measurement and carrier phase ionosphere-free combination for code ionosphere-free combination respectively) for smoothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SF:&lt;/b&gt; Use a Single Frequency (SF) carrier phase for smoothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;GC:&lt;/b&gt; Use a Graphic Combination (GC) for smoothing. This combination removes the ionosphere and has the pseudorange code noise halved. It is obtained with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;GC = (&lt;i&gt;Pseudorange&lt;/i&gt; + &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase&lt;/i&gt;)/2&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;IF:&lt;/b&gt; Use a carrier phase Ionosphere-Free (IF) combination for smoothing. It is computed with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;IF = (f1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase1&lt;/i&gt; -  f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; · &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase2&lt;/i&gt;)/(f1&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; - f2&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The frequency of the first carrier phase.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;  The frequency of the second carrier phase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;DF:&lt;/b&gt; Use a Divergence Free (DF) dual frequency combination for smoothing. This combination has no ionospheric divergence (hence the name) that occurs when using single frequency smoothing (see &lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;https://gssc.esa.int/navipedia/index.php/Code-Carrier_Divergence_Effect&lt;/font&gt; for details). It is computed with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DF = &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase1&lt;/i&gt; +2 · f&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;/(f&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt; - f&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;) · (&lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase1&lt;/i&gt; - &lt;i&gt;Carrier_phase2&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The frequency of the first carrier phase.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; The frequency of the second carrier phase.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="styleSheet">
                                           <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                          </property>
                                          <property name="text">
                                           <string>Smoothing with:</string>
                                          </property>
                                         </widget>
                                        </item>
