                                        </sizepolicy>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="toolTip">
                                        <string>&lt;b&gt;Excl. sat. before steady-state&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When using smoothing in DGNSS, wait for the steady-state (smoothing converges) until the satellite is used for the navigation solution. The steady-state is defined by 360 epochs of continuous smoothing, and is reset every time a cycle-slip occurs.&lt;br&gt;The steady-state is applied by default to the reference station measurements (in RTCM v3.x or RINEX observation files), but it can be applied also to the Rover. If this option is applied to both Rover and Reference station, each one will operate independently (that is, a cycle-slip in the rover will not affect the steady-state in the reference station and viceversa), but for a satellite to be used, in both sides the satellite must have reached steady-state.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="styleSheet">
                                        <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                       </property>
                                       <property name="text">
