                                </size>
                               </property>
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;TimeStamps&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Add timestamps to KML file. Each timestamp will have as the name the timestamp (in format YYYY DoY Seconds_of_Day), and in its description, the timestamp in format &quot;DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM:SS&quot;. All timestamps are in GPS time. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; This option applies to both KML and KML0 files.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="styleSheet">
                                <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>TimeStamps</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                             <item row="1" column="0">
                              <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxKMLRefStations">
                               <property name="sizePolicy">
                                <sizepolicy hsizetype="Fixed" vsizetype="Fixed">
                                 <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                                 <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                                </sizepolicy>
                               </property>
                               <property name="minimumSize">
                                <size>
                                 <width>0</width>
                                 <height>23</height>
                                </size>
                               </property>
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Add Reference Station&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If user is creating a KML file in DGNSS, add a PlaceMark (in its geographic position) for each reference station found during the processing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; This option applies to both KML and KML0 files.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="styleSheet">
                                <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>Add Reference Station</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                             <item row="1" column="1">
                              <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxKMLGeoid">
                               <property name="minimumSize">
                                <size>
                                 <width>0</width>
                                 <height>23</height>
                                </size>
                               </property>
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Geoid Height&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;GPS coordinate system, WGS84, uses a reference ellipsoid as an Earth model. In order to account the Earth irregularities, a geoid model is necessary. This geoid model provides (in ellipsoidal coordinates) the geoidal height (undulations) which is the difference between the geodetic height (h) to the orthometric height (H). Therefore, the equation to apply to the geoid model is:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;H&lt;sub&gt;orthometric&lt;/sub&gt; = h&lt;sub&gt;WGS84&lt;/sub&gt; - N&lt;sub&gt;EGM96&lt;/sub&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(m)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;H&lt;sub&gt;orthometric&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Height from the geoid earth surface (orthometric height).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;h&lt;sub&gt;WGS84&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Geodetic height provided from the GPS coordinates in the WGS84 coordinate system.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;N&lt;sub&gt;EGM96&lt;/sub&gt;:&lt;/b&gt; Geoidal height or difference between the geoid and the WGS84 reference ellipsoid.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;If this option is enabled, the height coordinate written in the KML file will be the orthometric height value (instead of the WGS84 geodetic height).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;The geoid model applied is EGM96 (with a resolution of 1ºx1º), which is the model applied in Google Earth.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The EGM96 model is provided through a grid of values in latitude and longitude. The final value applied is computed by linear interpolation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;EGM96 height correction values can vary from -106 to +85 metres.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;EGM96 grid values can be obtained from:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://earth-info.nga.mil/GandG/wgs84/gravitymod/egm96/egm96.html&quot;&gt;http://earth-info.nga.mil/GandG/wgs84/gravitymod/egm96/egm96.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; </string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="styleSheet">
                                <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>Geoid Height</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="checked">
                                <bool>true</bool>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
