                                <item row="0" column="0">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_KML_Decimation">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>0</width>
                                    <height>23</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;Decimation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set a decimation rate (with a maximum resolution of 0.0.0001 seconds) for the timestamps int the KML file (this decimation rate is independent from the data processing decimation rate).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set value to 0 to disable decimation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A KML file with too many timestamps may make the software reading the file hang or run very slow.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;This option applies to both KML and KML0 files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>Decimation</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="0" column="2">
                                 <widget class="QLabel" name="label_247">
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>(s)</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                                <item row="0" column="3">
                                 <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBox_KML_Range">
                                  <property name="minimumSize">
                                   <size>
                                    <width>0</width>
                                    <height>23</height>
                                   </size>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="toolTip">
                                   <string>&lt;b&gt;Range&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set a time range for timestamps. The user must give the start and ending epoch (in seconds of day of GPS time). When a range is set, only timestamp inside the range will be written to the KML file. Inside this range, the timestamp decimation also applies, but the first and last epoch of the range will also be written independently if these epochs match the decimation rate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &quot;-&quot; value in the start epoch means to start the range from the beginning of the file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &quot;-&quot; value in the ending epoch means to end the range at the end of the file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To account for files with multiple days, add 86400 seconds for each day passed (the starting day corresponds to the day of the first data read in the RINEX observation file).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In command line, the user can set any number of time ranges by using the parameter '-output:kml:tstamprange' as many times as necessary.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;This option applies to both KML and KML0 files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="styleSheet">
                                   <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                  </property>
                                  <property name="text">
                                   <string>Range</string>
                                  </property>
                                 </widget>
                                </item>
                               </layout>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
