                                   <item row="0" column="0">
                                    <widget class="QLabel" name="labelStfdESAMaxSatCombination">
                                     <property name="toolTip">
                                      <string>&lt;b&gt;Maximum Satellite Combinations:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the threshold (adimensional) of the maximum number of satellites a solution combination can have in order to be processed. This is for reducing processing time where there are many satellites available.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;gLAB will always loop through all possible combinations, but the ones with a higher number of satellites than this threshold will be skipped (i.e. no positioning error or protection levels are computed).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Skipping combinations with high number of satellites do not limit the detection of faulty combinations (positioning error equal or greater than protection levels), as usually faulty combination are the ones with smaller number of satellites. Moreover, once the faulty satellite(s) are detected with the smaller combinations (always processed), all other combinations with these faulty satellites are very likely to be faulty too.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                                     </property>
                                     <property name="styleSheet">
                                      <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                                     </property>
                                     <property name="text">
                                      <string>Maximum Satellite Combinations:</string>
                                     </property>
                                    </widget>
