                             <item row="2" column="0">
                              <widget class="QLabel" name="labelSummarySlidingWindow">
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>&lt;b&gt;Windows Size (Sliding/Fixed)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the window size to compute the continuity risk. The continuity risk is the probability to have a discontinuity (no solution under alarm limits) during a time window. There are two methods to compute the continuity risk:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sliding Window:&lt;/b&gt; When using a sliding window size of N samples, if in the current epoch a discontinuity occurs, all the previous N-1 samples (or the samples until the last discontinuity, whatever first occurs) plus the current one will be counted as epochs with continuty risk. Otherwise, if an epoch did not have a discontinuity, and during the following N samples no discontinuity occurred, that epoch will not be counted as epochs with discontinuity risk.&lt;br&gt;The continuity risk is computed by dividing the number of epochs with continuity risk (N&lt;sub&gt;EpochRisk&lt;/sub&gt;) divided by the number of epochs with solution under alarm limits (N&lt;sub&gt;EpochAvail&lt;/sub&gt;):&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Continuity Risk = N&lt;sub&gt;EpochRisk&lt;/sub&gt;/N&lt;sub&gt;EpochAvail&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fixed Window:&lt;/b&gt; When using a fixed window size of N samples, every time a discontinuity occurs, all the previous N epochs are counted as epochs with discontinuity, independently of the previous discontinuities. This is a more simple computation, but has the disadvantage that if several discontinuities occur in less than N epochs, the discontinuities will be counted more than once (this is typical in the SBAS coverage border), which may do that the total continuity risk become greater than 1. This effect can be mitigated by using large time spans. Moreover, if several discontinuities larger than the window size occur, the continuity risk value will be smaller compared to the sliding window continuity risk, as several epochs will not be counted to have discontinuities (the ones larger than the window size), and also due to that the continuity risk is computed using the total epochs processed, not the total epochs with solution.The continuity risk with fixed window is computed with the following formula:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Continuity Risk = CTI/MTBF = WindowSize·N&lt;sub&gt;Discontinuities&lt;/sub&gt;/N&lt;sub&gt;Processed_epochs&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;CTI:&lt;/b&gt; Continuity Time Interval, which is the size of the fixed window.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;MTBF:&lt;/b&gt; Mean Time Between Failures, which is computed as the total epochs processed (N&lt;sub&gt;Processed_epochs&lt;/sub&gt;) divided by the number of discontinuities (N&lt;sub&gt;Discontinuities&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;This formula is from IALA (International Association of Marine Aids to Navigation and Lighthouse Authorities), available in the following document:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.iala-aism.org/product/performance-and-monitoring-of-dgnss-services-in-the-frequency-band-283-5-325khz-1112/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&quot;&gt;http://www.iala-aism.org/product/performance-and-monitoring-of-dgnss-services-in-the-frequency-band-283-5-325khz-1112/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Sliding Window is the  method used in Airborne applications, while the Fixed Window is the method used for Maritime applications.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;gLAB will always compute the continuity risk with both methods.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;nobr&gt;See SBAS maps manual (&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help&amp;#8209;&gt;User manuals&amp;#8209;&gt;gLAB command line SBAS maps description&lt;/font&gt;)&lt;/nobr&gt; for more info on continuity risk computation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="styleSheet">
                                <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>Window Size (Sliding/Fixed)</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
