                           <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonNanosecondsUnitOutputClock">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Nanoseconds&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Print the estimated clock and DCB terms in the output messages in nanoseconds. The following messages will be affected:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;MODEL message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 28:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite clock correction [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 43:&lt;/b&gt; Inter system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 44:&lt;/b&gt; P1-C1 DCB (GPS only) [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 45:&lt;/b&gt; Total Group Delay (TGD) correction [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 46:&lt;/b&gt; Inter Signal Correction (if applied) [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 47:&lt;/b&gt; Computed DCB for single frequency and precise orbits (BeiDou only) [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 48:&lt;/b&gt; Sum of all DCB corrections applied (Field 44 + Field 45 + Field 46 + Field 47) [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 52-:&lt;/b&gt; Dual-frequency DCB computed for current dual-frequency combination [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;POSTFIT message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated inter-system clock bias [ns]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated satellite DCB [nanoseconds of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated receiver  DCB [nanoseconds of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;FILTER message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock offset [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; GPS inter-system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Galileo inter-system clock bias [ns]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS inter-system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; GEO inter-system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; BeiDou inter-system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; QZSS inter-system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; IRNSS inter-system clock bias [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;OUTPUT message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 34:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock offset [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 35:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock formal error [ns] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; If option &lt;i&gt;Print messages in gLAB v5 format&lt;/i&gt; is enabled, this option will have no effect.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Nanoseconds</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="0">
                           <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radioButtonMetresUnitOutputClock">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;Metres&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Print the estimated clock and DCB terms in the output messages in metres (this is the default). The following messages will be affected:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;MODEL message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 28:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite clock correction [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 43:&lt;/b&gt; Inter system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 44:&lt;/b&gt; P1-C1 DCB (GPS only) [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 45:&lt;/b&gt; Total Group Delay (TGD) correction [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 46:&lt;/b&gt; Inter Signal Correction (if applied) [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 47:&lt;/b&gt; Computed DCB for single frequency and precise orbits (BeiDou only) [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 48:&lt;/b&gt; Sum of all DCB corrections applied (Field 44 + Field 45 + Field 46 + Field 47) [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 52-:&lt;/b&gt; Dual-frequency DCB computed for current dual-frequency combination [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;POSTFIT message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated satellite DCB [metres of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated receiver  DCB [metres of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;FILTER message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock offset [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; GPS inter-system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Galileo inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS inter-system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; GEO inter-system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; BeiDou inter-system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; QZSS inter-system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; IRNSS inter-system clock bias [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;OUTPUT message:&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 34:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock offset [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 35:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock formal error [m] &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; If option &lt;i&gt;Print messages in gLAB v5 format&lt;/i&gt; is enabled, this option will have no effect.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Metres</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="2">
                           <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_169">
                            <property name="orientation">
                             <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
                            </property>
                            <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                             <size>
                              <width>0</width>
                              <height>20</height>
                             </size>
                            </property>
                           </spacer>
                          </item>
                         </layout>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                       <item row="3" column="0">
                        <spacer name="verticalSpacer_60">
                         <property name="orientation">
                          <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
                         </property>
                         <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                          <size>
                           <width>20</width>
                           <height>40</height>
                          </size>
                         </property>
                        </spacer>
                       </item>
                       <item row="0" column="0">
                        <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxCommonNavigationMessages">
                         <property name="sizePolicy">
                          <sizepolicy hsizetype="Minimum" vsizetype="Fixed">
                           <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                           <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                          </sizepolicy>
                         </property>
                         <property name="maximumSize">
                          <size>
                           <width>16777215</width>
                           <height>16777215</height>
                          </size>
                         </property>
                         <property name="font">
                          <font>
                           <pointsize>9</pointsize>
                           <weight>75</weight>
                           <bold>true</bold>
                          </font>
                         </property>
                         <property name="styleSheet">
                          <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
                         </property>
                         <property name="title">
                          <string>Output Messages</string>
                         </property>
                         <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_108">
                          <property name="leftMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="topMargin">
                           <number>9</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="rightMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="bottomMargin">
                           <number>6</number>
                          </property>
                          <property name="verticalSpacing">
                           <number>3</number>
                          </property>
                          <item row="6" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintPostfit">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;POSTFIT messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Postfilter values message. It provides the corrected prefits with the filter estimation. It is shown in each filter execution. Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'POSTFIT'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite block type&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; SVN (Space Vehicle Number)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite elevation [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite azimuth [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier for smoothing (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement-corrected model value (postfit) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Smoothed measurement value[m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Corrected model value with the filter estimations [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Only given for carrier phase measurements. It is the estimated carrier phase ambiguity [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated ionosphere [metres of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated satellite DCB [metres of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated receiver  DCB [metres of the signal frequency]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; POSTFIT   2019 025 85862.00 23:51:02.00 GPS 21 BLOCK_IIR-A       45   1    363   38.373   61.866          C1C          L1P         0.0803  37372802.1720  37372802.0569  37372801.9021         0.0000 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If no smoothing is enabled, field 15 will be a dash ('-') and field 18 will be 0.&lt;br/&gt; If smoothing is enabled, field 15 is the measurement used for smoothing.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print POSTFIT</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="3" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintSatsel">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;SATSEL messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Message with debug information of the reason why a satellite has been discarded (or selected) for processing. If multiple discard conditions are met in a single satellite, then a SATSEL message for each condition will be printed. Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'SATSEL'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Error code&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; &quot;Selected&quot; if satellite used or &quot;Discard reason&quot; if satellite unused&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; SATSEL    2019 025 85862.00 23:51:02.00 GPS 18  12 &quot;Steady-state operation not reached. 348 epochs passed, still 12 epochs to achieve 360&quot; &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; The error code in field 8 is a number which identifies the discard reason with a range from 1 to 120. Useful for parsing purposes.&lt;br/&gt;Field 9 will be always between quotes in order to ease parsing purposes.&lt;br/&gt;Fields 8 and 9 may have the following values:&lt;br&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;0:&lt;/b&gt; Selected&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1:&lt;/b&gt; Deselection forced&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement selection for rover not finished&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3:&lt;/b&gt; Measurements missing: measurements&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;4:&lt;/b&gt; SNR not met [&amp;lt;snr&amp;gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;5:&lt;/b&gt; Not enough consecutive samples (current &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;, minimum &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;6:&lt;/b&gt; Arc too short (&amp;lt;arclength&amp;gt;). Min arc length: &amp;lt;minarclength&amp;gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;7:&lt;/b&gt; Unconsistency of measurements&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;8:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier in MW detector&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;9:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier in LI detector&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;10:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier in IGF detector&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;11:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle-slip&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;12:&lt;/b&gt; Steady-state operation not reached. &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; epochs passed, still &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; epochs to achieve &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;19:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite missing in reference station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;20:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement selection for reference station not finished&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;21:&lt;/b&gt; Measurements missing in reference station: &amp;lt;measurements&amp;gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;22:&lt;/b&gt; SNR not met in reference station [&amp;lt;snr&amp;gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;23:&lt;/b&gt; Not enough consecutive samples in reference station (current &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;, minimum &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;24:&lt;/b&gt; Arc too short (&amp;lt;arclength&amp;gt;) in reference station. Min arc length: &amp;lt;minarclength&amp;gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;25:&lt;/b&gt; Unconsistency of measurements in reference station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;26:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier in MW detector in reference station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;27:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier in LI detector in reference station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;28:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier in IGF detector in reference station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;29:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle-slip in reference station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;40:&lt;/b&gt; No code measurement available for computing transmission time&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;41:&lt;/b&gt; No code and carrier phase measurement available for computing transmission time&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;42:&lt;/b&gt; Ephemerides unavailable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;43:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite phase center corrections unavailable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;44:&lt;/b&gt; GPS P1-C1 DCB unavailable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;45:&lt;/b&gt; DCBs unavailable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;46:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite under eclipse&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;47:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite was under eclipse&lt;value&gt; seconds ago&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;48:&lt;/b&gt; Elevation too low (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; degrees)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;49:&lt;/b&gt; Elevation too low (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; degrees) for applying weight 1/(sin(elev)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;50:&lt;/b&gt; Elevation too low (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; degrees) for applying weight 10&lt;sup&gt;(-SNR/10)&lt;/sup&gt;/(sin(elev)&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;51:&lt;/b&gt; No SNR available for computing the weight for measurement &amp;lt;measurements&amp;gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;52:&lt;/b&gt; Missing IONEX data&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;53:&lt;/b&gt; Missing FPPP data&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;54:&lt;/b&gt; SBAS iono unavailable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;55:&lt;/b&gt; URA value (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;) is equal or greater than the threshold (&amp;lt;threshold&amp;gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;56:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite is unhealthy &amp;lt;healthtext&amp;gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;57:&lt;/b&gt; No measurements selected for the filter due to missing frequency number (k)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;58:&lt;/b&gt; No measurements selected for the filter&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;59:&lt;/b&gt; No measurements selected for the filter&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;80:&lt;/b&gt; STEP detected (jump of &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; greater than &amp;lt;threshold&amp;gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;81:&lt;/b&gt; Prefit too high for measurement &amp;lt;meas&amp;gt; in comparison with other satellites&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;82:&lt;/b&gt; Prefit too high for measurement &amp;lt;meas&amp;gt;  in comparison with other satellites (threshold &amp;lt;threshold&amp;gt; metres)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;83:&lt;/b&gt; Prefit too different (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;) for measurement &amp;lt;meas&amp;gt;  with respect to the prefit median (&amp;lt;median&amp;gt;), threshold&lt;threshold&gt; metres&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;84:&lt;/b&gt; NeQuick ionosphere could not be computed&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;100:&lt;/b&gt; SBAS corrections unavailable (GEO &amp;lt;PRN&amp;gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;101:&lt;/b&gt; C1C measurement unavailable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;102:&lt;/b&gt; &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; constellation not monitored by SBAS (GEO &amp;lt;PRN&amp;gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;110:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;111:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections: Time out&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;112:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections: Excluded during the smoother conversion in the Reference Station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;113:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections: Excluded during the smoother conversion in the Rover Station&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;114:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections: IODE from BRDC and RTCM do not match&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;115:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections: Excluded due to differential correction is too large&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;116:&lt;/b&gt; No DGNSS corrections: Epoch in reference station (last read &amp;lt;ref_station_epoch&amp;gt;) cannot be aligned with rover&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; Error codes 1 to 18 are for rover preprocessing, 19 to 39 for reference station preprocessing, 40 to 79 for modelling, 80 to 99 for the filter, 100 to 109 for SBAS and 110 to 120 for DGNSS.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print SATSEL</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="3" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintInput">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;INPUT messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Input data message. It is shown after an epoch is read, decimated and added user-defined error It contains the measurements for each satellite for this epoch Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE&lt;/b&gt;: INPUT message is deprecated, use MEAS message instead.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'INPUT'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; Doy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;For GPS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; C1 (C1C) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; P1 (C1P) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; P2 (C2P) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; L1 (L1P) (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; L2 (L2P) (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;For Galileo:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; C1A [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; C1B [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; C1C [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; C7Q [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; C8Q [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; L1A (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; L1B (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; L1C (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; L7Q (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; L8Q (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;For GLONASS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; C1 (C1C) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; C2 (C2C) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; L1 (L1P) (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; L2 (L2P) (prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;For GEO:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; C1 (C1C) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt;INPUT     2006 200     0.00 00:00:00.00 GPS 19   1      1  23119003.9020  23119002.6110  23119004.0750  23119002.7507  23119004.0925&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print INPUT</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="0" column="0" colspan="2">
                           <widget class="QFrame" name="frame_15">
                            <property name="sizePolicy">
                             <sizepolicy hsizetype="Minimum" vsizetype="Fixed">
                              <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                              <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                             </sizepolicy>
                            </property>
                            <property name="frameShape">
                             <enum>QFrame::NoFrame</enum>
                            </property>
                            <property name="frameShadow">
                             <enum>QFrame::Raised</enum>
                            </property>
                            <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_110">
                             <property name="leftMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="topMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="rightMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <property name="bottomMargin">
                              <number>0</number>
                             </property>
                             <item row="0" column="0">
                              <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonCommonNavigationMessagesAll">
                               <property name="enabled">
                                <bool>true</bool>
                               </property>
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>Select all output messages.</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>All</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                             <item row="0" column="1">
                              <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonCommonNavigationMessagesNone">
                               <property name="toolTip">
                                <string>Unselect all output messages.</string>
                               </property>
                               <property name="text">
                                <string>None</string>
                               </property>
                              </widget>
                             </item>
                            </layout>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="5" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintSFCS">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;SFCSDATA messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Internal values used in the computation of the single frequency carrier minus code cycle-slip detector Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'SFCSDATA'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; Doy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the carrier minus code combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Code measurement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Carrier phase measurement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Difference between current code measurement and previous epoch code measurement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Difference between current carrier phase measurement and previous epoch carrier phase measurement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between fields 13 and 14 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Mean value of the difference between code and carrier phase measurement inside the sliding window [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Sigma value of the difference between code and carrier phase measurement inside the sliding window [m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Computed difference. It is the squared value of (field 12 minus field 11 minus field 16) squared [m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Computed threshold. It is the minimum value between the current sigma (field 17) and the initial sigma multiplied by the k factor [m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Maximum threshold for declaring a measurement unconsistent [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Unconsistency flag. If an unconsistency is found, value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle-slip flag. If a cycle-slip is found, value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; SFCSDATA 2019 031 61530.00 17:05:30.00 GAL 24   1     2 C8Q-L8Q  24042582.3540  24042582.4685    -10183.8650    -10183.8300         0.0350      0.0795      9.0000      0.0012    225.0000  20.0000 0 0 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; An unconsistency is triggered when field 15 is greater than field 20. In this case, all satellites samples are skipped (it is considered as a data gap but without triggering N-consecutive check) Consistency check cannot be triggered two consecutive epochs.&lt;br/&gt; A cycle-slip is triggered when field 18 is greater than field 19.&lt;br/&gt; The cycle-slip flag in field 22 will only be enabled if the single frequency detector detects a cycle-slip, but not if another cycle-slip running in parallel detects a cycle-slip trigger and the single frequency detector doesn't.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print SFCSDATA</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="2" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintUsererror">
                            <property name="minimumSize">
                             <size>
                              <width>0</width>
                              <height>0</height>
                             </size>
                            </property>
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;USERADDEDERROR (only when user-defined error file is given)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;User-defined error added to measurements before cycle-slip detection and smoothing (or after if option &quot;Insert User Added Error after preprocessing&quot; is enabled).  Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'USERADDEDERROR'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GPS week&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; Time of week&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; PRN&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Raw measurement (phase measurements are prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Raw measurement plus total user-defined error (phase measurements are prealigned) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of active user-defined error functions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Total user-defined error [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Number of active Step function error&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Step function error value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Number of active Ramp function error&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Ramp function error value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Number of active Sinusoidal function error&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Sinusoidal function error value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Number of active AWGN (Additive White Gaussian Noise) function error&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; AWGN function error value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt;USERADDEDERROR   2015 161     0.00 00:00:00.00 1848 259200.00 GPS   4 C1C  23140309.8200  23140314.8200  1         5.0000  1         5.0000  0         0.0000  0         0.0000  0         0.0000&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print USERADDEDERROR</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="7" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintFilter">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;FILTER messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Filter solution message. This message provides direct information on the filter estimates. It is shown in each filter execution. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'FILTER'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; Constellation used as reference clock&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; Number of inter-sytem clock bias estimated in the filter&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Number of unknowns estimated in the filter&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver X position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Y position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Z position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock offset [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; GPS inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Galileo inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; GEO inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; BeiDou inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; QZSS inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; IRNSS inter-system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If troposphere is estimated in the filter, the next field will appear:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Zenith Tropospheric Delay (vertical wet component) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; FILTER    2018 130     7.00 00:00:07.00 GPS 3 38   3924697.5020    301125.3025   5001905.0392       -10.2643         0.0000         1.8811         5.6634         0.0000         3.0240         0.0000         0.0000         2.4869&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If any of the inter-system clock biases in fields 13-19 is not estimated in the filter, its value will be 0.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print FILTER</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintPrefit">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;PREFIT messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Prefilter values message. It provides the measurement-model values. It is shown in each filter execution. Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'PREFIT'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite block type&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; SVN (Space Vehicle Number)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite elevation [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite azimuth [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier for smoothing (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement-model value (prefit) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Smoothed measurement value[m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Model value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; X-partial derivative (-X component of the satellite line-of-sight vector)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Y-partial derivative (-Y component of the satellite line-of-sight vector)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Z-partial derivative (-Z component of the satellite line-of-sight vector)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; T-partial derivative&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Standard deviation of the measurement  (for the filter) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 25:&lt;/b&gt; Troposphere wet mapping&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 26:&lt;/b&gt; Wavelength of the measurement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 27:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS frequency number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; PREFIT    2019 025 85862.00 23:51:02.00 GPS 15 BLOCK_IIR-M       55   1    363    9.133   56.540          C1C          L1P  14508353.7082  39110017.2878  39110017.0467  24601663.5797         0.4131        -0.7708        -0.4850         1.0000    2.7740    6.0697    0.1903  0 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If no smoothing is enabled, field 15 will be a dash ('-'), field 18 will be 0 and Field 16 = Field 17 - Field 19.&lt;br/&gt; If smoothing is enabled, field 15 is the measurement used for smoothing, field 18 will be the smoothed value and Field 16 = Field 18 - Field 19.&lt;br/&gt; Field 26 is the frequency wavelength. When a iono-free combination is used, the wavelength is computed with the formula 'lambda=c/(f1+f2)'.&lt;br/&gt; Field 27 is the GLONASS frequency number 'k' read from navigation message. For other constellations, value is 0.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print PREFIT</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="6" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintMWCS">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;MWCSDATA messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Internal values used in the computation of the Melbourne-Wubbena cycle-slip detector Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'MWCSDATA'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; Doy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the Melbourne-Wubbena combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; First Code measurement for building the narrow lane combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Second Code measurement for building the narrow lane combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; First Carrier phase measurement the wide lane combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Second Carrier phase measurement the wide lane combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Melbourne-Wubbena combination with current measurements [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Mean value of Melbourne-Wubbena in the current arc [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Mean value of Melbourne-Wubbena in the sliding window [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Sigma value of Melbourne-Wubbena in the current arc [m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between field 15 and field 16 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between field 15 and field 17 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Computed threshold. It is the square root of field 18 by the k factor [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Minimum standard deviation provided by parameter [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier flag. If an outlier is declared , value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle-slip flag. If a cycle-slip is found, value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; MWCSDATA 2019 031 61660.00 17:07:40.00 GAL 24   2    12 C6C-C8Q-L6C-L8Q  24210219.9290  24210239.3620  24210219.9516  24210239.7865   281.2079   281.1575   281.1575     0.3692      0.0503      0.0503      3.0381   0.8000 0 0 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; A cycle-slip is triggered when fields 19 and 20 are greater than field 21 and the square root of field 18 is smaller than field 22 or if field 18 is greater than ten times field 22.&lt;br/&gt; The first time a cycle-slip is detected, the samples are considered as 'outlier' and samples are skipped (it is considered as data gap but without triggering N-consecutive check). If the next sample a cycle-slip is triggered, then a new arc is declared. Otherwise, if no cycle-slip is detected the next epoch, the arc continues with the previous epoch skipped.&lt;br/&gt; The cycle-slip flag in field 24 will only be enabled if the Melbourne-Wubbena detector detects a cycle-slip, but not if another cycle-slip running in parallel detects a cycle-slip trigger and the Melbourne-Wubbena detector doesn't.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print MWCSDATA</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="2" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintModel">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;MODEL messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Model break down message. It is shown when a model can be fully computed for each measurement. Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. Satellite coordinates are in WGS84 system. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'MODEL'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite block type&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; SVN (Space Vehicle Number)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite elevation [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite azimuth [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Broadcast message type used for orbit computation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; IOD of the broadcast message used for orbit computation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS frequency number (k)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Leap seconds (GLONASS) or BeiDou to GPS time offset [s]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Measured value [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Signal flight time [sec]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite X position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite Y position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite Z position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite X velocity [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 25:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite Y velocity [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 26:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite Z velocity [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 27:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite-receiver geometric distance [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 28:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite clock correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 29:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite phase centre projection [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 30:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite phase centre variation projection [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 31:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver phase centre projection [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 32:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver phase centre variation projection [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 33:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Antenna Reference Point (ARP) projection [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 34:&lt;/b&gt; Relativity correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 35:&lt;/b&gt; Wind-up correction [m] (for carrier phase measurements)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 36:&lt;/b&gt; Troposphere nominal correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 37:&lt;/b&gt; Ionosphere correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 38:&lt;/b&gt; Gravitational delay correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 39:&lt;/b&gt; Solid tides correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 40:&lt;/b&gt; (Reserved for future fields)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 41:&lt;/b&gt; (Reserved for future fields)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 42:&lt;/b&gt; (Reserved for future fields)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 43:&lt;/b&gt; Inter system clock bias [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 44:&lt;/b&gt; P1-C1 DCB (GPS only) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 45:&lt;/b&gt; Total Group Delay (TGD) correction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 46:&lt;/b&gt; Inter Signal Correction (if applied) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 47:&lt;/b&gt; Computed DCB for single frequency and precise orbits (BeiDou only) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 48:&lt;/b&gt; Sum of all DCB corrections applied (Field 44 + Field 45 + Field 46 + Field 47) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 49:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement SNR (Signal to Noise Ratio) [dbHz]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 50:&lt;/b&gt; Full model value (except for dual-frequency DCB)[m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If measurement needs to be applied a dual-frequency DCB, for each dual frequency combination where the measurement is used, the following three fields will be provided:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 51-:&lt;/b&gt; Measurements used for the dual frequency combination&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 52-:&lt;/b&gt; Dual-frequency DCB computed for current dual-frequency combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 53-:&lt;/b&gt; Full model value with dual-frequency DCB applied [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; MODEL     2019 025 85862.00 23:51:02.00 GPS 15 BLOCK_IIR-M       55   1    363    9.133   56.540 C1C      LNAV    1  0  0 39110018.66000         0.0817  -5849446.9671  19529241.5438  16560946.2782     -1025.8786     -1939.4413      1934.8478  24502508.9762     99139.2638   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000  -0.00000   1.12021   0.00000  13.46324   1.71706   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000   0.00000  -3.21084   0.00000   0.00000  -3.21084   53.000  24601663.5797 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If precise products are used, fields 15 and 16 will have the fixed values 'SP3' and '-1' respectively.&lt;br/&gt; Field 18, for GLONASS satellites will have the number of leap seconds. For BeiDou satellites, the value will be the fixed offset to GPS. For other constellations value is 0.&lt;br/&gt; The satellite coordinates (fields 21-26) are given in the transmission epoch if the model of the signal transmission time is enabled (if it is disabled, they are given in the reception time). The coordinates are relative to the antenna phase centre or satellite mass centre, depending on the products input: &lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;* Broadcast: Antenna Phase Centre&lt;br/&gt;* Precise: Satellite Mass Centre&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; Field 19 is the direct measurement (as in the RINEX file), but scaled to metres for carrier phase measurements. Field 48 is the model computed for this measurement, which is the direct sum of fields 27 to 47.&lt;br/&gt; When the '*' appears in field 1, it is due to smoothed code of the satellite has not reached steady-state, a SBAS processing mode switch or SBAS GEO switch. When a mode or GEO switch occurs, the SBAS corrections have to be computed again.&lt;br/&gt; The SNR value in field 49 may be any of these values (in this order): the &quot;S&quot; measurement in the observation file, or if it is not present, it will be the SNR flag in the current measurement (converted to numerical value).&lt;br/&gt;If no SNR is available, 999 will be printed in this field.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print MODEL</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="8" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintOutput">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;OUTPUT messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Receiver solution message. This message provides the estimated receiver position in WGS84 system. It is shown in each filter execution. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'OUTPUT'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; Processing mode indicator&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; Processing direction indicator&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Number of satellites used in the navigation solution&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Number of constellations used in the navigation solution&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; List of constellations used in the filter (separated by dashes ('-')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Square root of the sum of the X, Y and Z components of the covariance matrix. This is a measure of the convergence of the filter&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver X position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Y position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Z position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver X position - Nominal a priori X position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Y position - Nominal a priori Y position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Z position - Nominal a priori Z position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver X formal error [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Y formal error [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Z formal error [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver latitude [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver longitude [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver height [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver North difference in relation to nominal a priori position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 25:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver East difference in relation to nominal a priori position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 26:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver Up difference in relation to nominal a priori position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 27:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver formal error in North direction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 28:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver formal error in East direction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 29:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver formal error in Up direction [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 30:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver horizontal difference in relation to nominal a priori position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 31:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver vertical difference in relation to nominal a priori position (absolute value of the error in Up direction) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 32:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver 3D difference in relation to nominal a priori position [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 33:&lt;/b&gt; Constellation used as reference clock&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 34:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock offset [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 35:&lt;/b&gt; Receiver clock formal error [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 36:&lt;/b&gt; Geometric Dilution of Precision (GDOP)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 37:&lt;/b&gt; Positioning Dilution of Precision (PDOP)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 38:&lt;/b&gt; Time Dilution of Precision (TDOP)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 39:&lt;/b&gt; Horizontal Dilution of Precision (HDOP)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 40:&lt;/b&gt; Vertical Dilution of Precision (VDOP)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 41:&lt;/b&gt; Zenith Tropospheric Delay (including nominal value) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 42:&lt;/b&gt; Zenith Tropospheric Delay (excluding nominal value) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 43:&lt;/b&gt; Zenith Tropospheric Delay formal error [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; OUTPUT    2019 099 86100.00 23:55:00.00 1 0 30 5 GPS+GAL+GLO+BDS+QZS    0.0040  -6257572.1031    950333.4266    785215.5957     0.0265    -0.0182    -0.0044     0.0036     0.0016     0.0009    7.119151644  171.364514044        33.6692    -0.0008     0.0140    -0.0292     0.0013     0.0015     0.0035 GPS         1.4242         0.0573    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000     2.7166     0.3260     0.0035 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; The fields 41, 42 and 43 will be zero if troposphere is not estimated (only estimated in PPP mode).&lt;br/&gt; Processing mode indicator in field 6 may have the following values: &lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;0 -&gt; SPP&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1 -&gt; PPP&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2 -&gt; Reserved&lt;br&gt;3 -&gt; Reserved&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print OUTPUT</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="5" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintEpochsat">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;EPOCHSAT messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Message with the satellites used to compute the solution. It is shown for each measurement in the filter plus an additional one with the whole measurements (shown at the end). Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'EPOCHSAT'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; Measurement identifier used for smoothing (as string)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of satellites selected and unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; GPS constellation letter     ('G')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of GPS     satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Galileo constellation letter ('E')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of Galileo satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS constellation letter ('R')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of GLONASS satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; GEO constellation letter     ('S')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of GEO     satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; BeiDou constellation letter  ('C')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of BeiDou  satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; QZSS constellation letter    ('J')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of QZSS    satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; IRNSS constellation letter   ('I')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of IRNSS   satellites selected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 25:&lt;/b&gt; GPS constellation letter     ('G')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 26:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of GPS     satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 27:&lt;/b&gt; Galileo constellation letter ('E')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 28:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of Galileo satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 29:&lt;/b&gt; GLONASS constellation letter ('R')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 30:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of GLONASS satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 31:&lt;/b&gt; GEO constellation letter     ('S')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 32:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of GEO     satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 33:&lt;/b&gt; BeiDou constellation letter  ('C')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 34:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of BeiDou  satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 35:&lt;/b&gt; QZSS constellation letter    ('J')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 36:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of QZSS    satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 37:&lt;/b&gt; IRNSS constellation letter   ('I')&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 38:&lt;/b&gt; Total number of IRNSS   satellites unselected for the current measurement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 39-:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite list. Each following column is a '+' or '-' sign, the satellite system and the PRN identifier. The '+' sign indicates that the satellite has been used in the solution computation. The '-' sign indicates that the satellite has not been used in the solution computation. The satellite list will show first all the satellites with the '+' and after the ones with the '-' sign (ordered by constellation).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; EPOCHSAT  2018 130 86280.00 23:58:00.00          C5X            - 20  +8 G  4 E  4 R  0 S  0 C  0 J  0 I  0 -12 G 10 E  1 R  0 S  0 C  0 J  1 I  0 +G01 +G09 +G06 +G03 +E05 +E24 +E26 +E03 -G31 -G12 -G23 -G17 -G18 -G14 -G25 -G11 -G19 -G22 -E08 -J02 &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; If the EPOCHSAT line refers to all measurements used in the filter, field 6 will have the value &quot;ALL&quot;.&lt;br&gt; If no smoothing is enabled, field 7 will be a dash ('-').&lt;br&gt; If smoothing is enabled, field 7 is the measurement used for smoothing.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print EPOCHSAT</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="8" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintIGFCS">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;IGFCSDATA messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Internal values used in the computation of the iono-geometry-free cycle-slip detector Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'IGFCSDATA'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; Doy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the iono-geometry-free combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; First Carrier phase measurement for building the iono-geometry-free combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Second Carrier phase measurement for building the iono-geometry-free combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Third Carrier phase measurement for building the iono-geometry-free combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Fourth Carrier phase measurement for building the iono-geometry-free combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; First IGF measurement saved in the IGF buffer sliding window [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; IGF combination with current measurements [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between field 15 and field 16 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated IGF value using a second degree least square adjustement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between field 16 and field 18 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of two times the residual of the IGF estimation (threshold for maximum value of field 19) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Threshold for maximum value of field 17&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Threshold for maximum value of field 19&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 23:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier flag. If an outlier is declared , value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 24:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle-slip flag. If a cycle-slip is found, value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; If option '-pre:cs:igf:minnoise' is set, the IGF is computed with the following formula: IGF = Alpha·L1 + Beta·L2 + Gamma·L3 With this option, field 14 will be 999999.0000, as only three measurements are used. The next three fields are the computed values for Alpha, Beta and Gamma (adimensional factors)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 25:&lt;/b&gt; Alpha factor. To be multiplied with field 11&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 26:&lt;/b&gt; Beta factor. To be multiplied with field 12&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 27:&lt;/b&gt; Gamma factor. To be multiplied with field 13&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; IGFCSDATA 2019 031 61640.00 17:07:20.00 GAL 26   1    13 L1C-L5Q-L6C-L8Q  23994292.6633  23994294.1164  23994293.2320  23994294.0525   3.0103   3.0243   0.0140      3.0077      0.0166      0.0020   1.0000   0.1057 0 0 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; A cycle-slip is triggered when field 17 is greater than field 21 or field 19 is greater than fields 20 and 22. If a cycle-slip is declared with the first condition, no outlier is declared, as it is a check for large phase jumps. If a cycle-slip triggers with the second condition, an outlier is declared. If in the next epoch a cycle-slip is triggered, then a new arc is declared. Otherwise, if no cycle-slip is detected the next epoch, the arc continues with the previous epoch skipped.&lt;br/&gt; The cycle-slip flag in field 24 will only be enabled if the iono-geometry-free detector detects a cycle-slip, but not if another cycle-slip running in parallel detects a cycle-slip trigger and the iono-geometry-free detector doesn't.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print IGFCSDATA</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="1" column="1">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintMeas">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;MEAS messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Information of the input measurements in a variable format, and azimuth/elevation of the satellite. It is written after modelling the message. Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'MEAS'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite block type&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; SVN (Space Vehicle Number)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite elevation [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; Satellite azimuth [degrees]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Number of measurements&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements included&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16-:&lt;/b&gt; Each following column is the value of the measurement specified in Field 13&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; MEAS      2019 182     0.00 00:00:00.00 GPS 26       BLOCK_IIF   71   1      1   29.689  -85.121 15 C1C:L1C:S1C:C1W:L1W:S1W:C2X:L2X:S2X:C2W:L2W:S2W:C5X:L5X:S5X  22797916.2960  22797916.3449 44.750  22797915.8300  22797915.9666 34.250 22797918.6020  22797918.7745 46.500  22797918.6990  22797918.7748 34.250  22797919.1480  22797919.3039 53.000 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;If there is no data available on azimuth and elevation, the fields 10 and 11 will be fixed to zero.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;User can define the measurements to be printed (in fields 14 and onwards) on a per satellite basis, by using the parameter '-print:meas:select'.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The MEAS message can be used as a way to convert a RINEX file to a columnar text file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In command line only, there is the mode &quot;show Input&quot;, where if only a RINEX observation file is provided, gLAB will just print INFO, MEAS and cycle-slip messages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print MEAS</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="1" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintInfo">
                            <property name="acceptDrops">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;INFO messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;INFO messages are shown at several points in the program and provide information on the program configuration, events and problems it may encounter, which are:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;At the start of the file, showing information about gLAB configuration.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;An inconsistent clock update on the receiver.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A data gap in the RINEX observation file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A change in the a priori receiver coordinates (only when receiver coordinates are computed by gLAB).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The new position to be used from the reference position file (only when a reference file is provided).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;No solution was computed, along with the reason for not being able to compute the solution (not enough satellites available, singular geometry matrix or DOP too high).&lt;li&gt;In SBAS processing, the elevation of each GEO and the one selected (if GEO selection with highest elevation is enabled).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In SBAS processing, a GEO or mode switch.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In SBAS processing, if option '-mode:selectbestgeo' is enabled, in each epoch, for each GEO which a solution can be computed, the GEO PRN, its protection levels and a message if the GEO was selected is printed. The selected GEO will be always the last one.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In DGNSS processing, a switch from DGNSS to SPP solution mode.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In DGNSS processing, a data gap in the reference station RINEX observation file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print INFO</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>true</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="7" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintLICS">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;LICSDATA messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Internal values used in the computation of the geometry-free cycle-slip detector Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'LICSDATA'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; Doy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS System&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN satellite identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; Arc number&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; Arc length&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the geometry-free combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; First Carrier phase measurement for building the geometry-free combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; Second Carrier phase measurement for building the geometry-free combination [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; First LI measurement saved in the LI buffer sliding window [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; LI combination with current measurements [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 15:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between field 13 and field 14 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 16:&lt;/b&gt; Estimated LI value using a second degree least square adjustement [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 17:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between field 14 and field 16 [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 18:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of two times the residual of the LI estimation (threshold for maximum value of field 17) [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 19:&lt;/b&gt; Threshold for maximum value of field 15&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 20:&lt;/b&gt; Threshold for maximum value of field 17&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 21:&lt;/b&gt; Outlier flag. If an outlier is declared , value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 22:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle-slip flag. If a cycle-slip is found, value is '1'. In all other cases, value is '0'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; SFCSDATA 2019 031 61530.00 17:05:30.00 GAL 24   1     2 C8Q-L8Q  24042582.3540  24042582.4685    -10183.8650    -10183.8300         0.0350      0.0795      9.0000      0.0012    225.0000  20.0000 0 0 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; A cycle-slip is triggered when field 15 is greater than field 19 or field 17 is greater than fields 18 and 20. If a cycle-slip is declared with the first condition, no outlier is declared, as it is a check for large phase jumps. If a cycle-slip triggers with the second condition, an outlier is declared. If in the next epoch a cycle-slip is triggered, then a new arc is declared. Otherwise, if no cycle-slip is detected the next epoch, the arc continues with the previous epoch skipped.&lt;br/&gt; The cycle-slip flag in field 22 will only be enabled if the geometry-free detector detects a cycle-slip, but not if another cycle-slip running in parallel detects a cycle-slip trigger and the geometry-free detector doesn't.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print LICSDATA</string>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                          <item row="4" column="0">
                           <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBoxPrintCS">
                            <property name="toolTip">
                             <string>&lt;b&gt;CS messages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Cycle-slip message information. It is shown when a cycle-slip is found by any detector. A line will be printed for each CS detector that has found a CS. The first 7 fields are common, afterwards, there are five possible different CS messages depending on the cycle-slip detector activated. Messages will be sorted by constellation, with this order: GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, GEO, BeiDou, QZSS, IRNSS. All time tags are in GPS time.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 1:&lt;/b&gt; 'CS'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 2:&lt;/b&gt; Year&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 3:&lt;/b&gt; DoY&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 4:&lt;/b&gt; Seconds of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 5:&lt;/b&gt; Time of day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 6:&lt;/b&gt; GNSS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 7:&lt;/b&gt; PRN&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data gap detector:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; '-'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; 'DATA_GAP'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Difference of time between current and last available epochs [s]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; 'THRESHOLD'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; Maximum time allowed data gap threshold [s]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; CS       2014 288 44997.00 12:29:57.00 GPS 32 - DATA_GAP = 45.00 THRESHOLD = 40.00 &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loss of Lock Indicator:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; '-'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; 'LLI'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements and its LLI flag value&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; CS       2019 031 72340.00 20:05:40.00 GPS  9 - LLI L1C-1 L2L-1 L5Q-1 &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Single frequency (SF) detector:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the carrier minus code combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; 'SF'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Squared value of carrier phase minus code minus the current arc mean [m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; 'THRESHOLD'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; SF threshold [m&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; CS       2019 032 19600.00 05:26:40.00 GAL  1 C5Q-L5Q SF = 39.8400 THRESHOLD = 25.4303 &lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Melbourne-Wubbena (MW) detector:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the MW combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; 'MW'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between the current MW and the mean value of MW of current arc [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; 'THRESHOLD'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; MW threshold [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; CS       2019 032 10780.00 02:59:40.00 GPS 10 C1C-C5Q-L1C-L5Q MW = 1.1744 THRESHOLD = 1.1304 &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Geometry-free carrier phase (LI) detector:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the LI combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; 'LI'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between the computed LI and the measured LI. If LI could not be estimated, value will be '999999.0000' [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; 'THRESHOLD'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; LI threshold [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; CS       2019 032 17310.00 04:48:30.00 GPS 32 L1C-L2W LI = 0.1134 THRESHOLD = 0.0528 &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Iono-geometry-free carrier phase (IGF) detector:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 8:&lt;/b&gt; List of measurements used to build the IGF combination, separated by dashes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 9:&lt;/b&gt; 'IGF'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 10:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 11:&lt;/b&gt; Absolute value of the difference between the computed IGF and the measured IGF. If IGF could not be estimated, value will be '999999.0000' [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 12:&lt;/b&gt; 'THRESHOLD'&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 13:&lt;/b&gt; '='&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field 14:&lt;/b&gt; IGF threshold [m]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sample:&lt;/b&gt; CS       2019 032 17310.00 04:48:30.00 GPS 32 L1C-L2W LI = 0.1134 THRESHOLD = 0.0528 &lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="styleSheet">
                             <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="text">
                             <string>Print CS (Cycle-slip)</string>
                            </property>
                            <property name="checked">
                             <bool>false</bool>
                            </property>
                           </widget>
                          </item>
                         </layout>
                        </widget>
                       </item>
                      </layout>
                     </widget>
                    </item>
