          <widget class="QWidget" name="pageAnalysis">
           <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_168">
            <item row="2" column="0">
             <spacer name="verticalSpacer_8">
              <property name="orientation">
               <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
               <size>
                <width>20</width>
                <height>0</height>
               </size>
              </property>
             </spacer>
            </item>
            <item row="0" column="0">
             <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBoxTemplates">
              <property name="font">
               <font>
                <weight>75</weight>
                <bold>true</bold>
               </font>
              </property>
              <property name="styleSheet">
               <string notr="true">QGroupBox {color: rgb(45, 36, 90);}</string>
              </property>
              <property name="title">
               <string>Templates</string>
              </property>
              <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_167">
               <property name="spacing">
                <number>10</number>
               </property>
               <item row="0" column="1">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateHorizontalError">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Horizontal positioning error&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Horizontal positioning error&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the North vs East position error components. This provides an insight of the horizontal dispersion and bias of the errors. To see more details on how the error is computed, see the &lt;i&gt;NEU positioning error&lt;/i&gt; button template.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Horizontal Positioning Error</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="0" column="0">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateNeuPositioningError">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: NEU positioning error&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;NEU position error&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the three components (North, East and Up) of the error of the receiver positioning obtained by the filter. This error is computed by the difference between the direct filter estimation and the &lt;i&gt;A priori Receiver Position&lt;/i&gt; in the &lt;i&gt;Input&lt;/i&gt; section of &lt;i&gt;Calculus&lt;/i&gt;. Thence to obtain a reliable error estimation, this a priori position should be precise.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you do not have any precise position of the receiver, you can obtain it by doing a PPP processing (&lt;i&gt;SP3&lt;/i&gt;/&lt;i&gt;Static&lt;/i&gt;/&lt;i&gt;Dual-frequency&lt;/i&gt;/&lt;i&gt;Pseudorange+Carrier phase&lt;/i&gt;). The XYZ position (fields 6 to 8 of &lt;i&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/i&gt; message) of the last epoch should have an accuracy in the order of the centimetre, and can be used as a good reference position.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>NEU Positioning Error</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="autoDefault">
                  <bool>false</bool>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                 <property name="flat">
                  <bool>false</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="1" column="3">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateMeasurementMultipath">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Measurements Multipath/Noise&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Measurements Multipath/Noise&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the measurement multipath for: &lt;i&gt;C1 code measurement, the Geometry-Free combination, the Melbourne-Wübenna and the GRAPHIC combination.&lt;/i&gt; In addition to these combinations, raw measurements present in the file can also be plotted.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Measurement Multipath/Noise</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="0" column="2">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateDOP">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Dilution Of Precision (DOP)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;DOP&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print Geometric Dilution of Precision (GDOP), Horizontal Dilution of Precision (HDOP), Vertical Dilution of Precision (VDOP), Time Dilution of Precision (TDOP). &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This computations take into account the geometry matrix (G), which is linked only to the receiver-satellite(s) ray geometry. This factor impacts the accuracy of the filter solution.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Dilution Of Precision</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="1" column="0">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateModelComponents">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Model components&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Model components&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print a component of the model as a function of time. By default, it selects the &lt;b&gt;Relativity effect&lt;/b&gt;, but it can easily be chosen which model to print, by choosing it in the &lt;i&gt;Y Column&lt;/i&gt; option.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Model Components</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="1" column="1">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplatePrefitResiduals">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Prefit residuals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Prefit residuals&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the measurement-model values &lt;b&gt;prefits&lt;/b&gt;, which is the input to each filter execution as a function of time. It prints both pseudorange and carrier phase prefits.&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; In general Prefit = Measurement - Model, but this is no longer true when using smoothing, as the first is the raw measurement without smoothing, but the second term takes smoothing into account.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Prefit Residuals</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="1" column="2">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplatePostfitResiduals">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Postfit residuals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Postfit residuals&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the &lt;b&gt;filter residuals&lt;/b&gt; (postfits) as a function of the satellite elevation. It prints both pseudorange and carrier phase postfits. This plot allows to observe the dependence of residuals from elevation. In general, carrier phase residuals will be quite independent from elevation, and pseudorange residuals can have a large dependence on elevation.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Posfit Residuals</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="0" column="3">
                <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateSatelliteSkyplot">
                 <property name="minimumSize">
                  <size>
                   <width>0</width>
                   <height>30</height>
                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Satellite skyplot&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Satellite skyplot&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the elevation/azimuth of the satellites in a skyplot, being the centre of the plot the zenith of the satellite, and the extremes, the lower elevations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a special plot which makes use of sin and cos in the &lt;i&gt;X column&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;Y column&lt;/i&gt; to obtain a polar plot. You can use it as example for other operations in the columns.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Satellite Skyplot</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="default">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item row="2" column="0" colspan="4">
                <widget class="QStackedWidget" name="stackedWidgetTemplates">
                 <property name="sizePolicy">
                  <sizepolicy hsizetype="Preferred" vsizetype="Fixed">
                   <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                   <verstretch>0</verstretch>
                  </sizepolicy>
                 </property>
                 <property name="currentIndex">
                  <number>1</number>
                 </property>
                 <widget class="QWidget" name="page_59">
                  <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_182">
                   <property name="leftMargin">
                    <number>0</number>
                   </property>
                   <property name="topMargin">
                    <number>0</number>
                   </property>
                   <property name="rightMargin">
                    <number>0</number>
