                      <item row="3" column="0">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonStanfordESAPlot">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Stanford-ESA&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Stanford-ESA&lt;/i&gt; is a special template, as the input data is read from the &lt;i&gt;Stanford-ESA Plot File&lt;/i&gt; (which the user has to enable in the OUTPUT section). In the Stanford-ESA, instead of the ocurrences which appear in the navigation solution, it is shown all the ocurrences with all possible combinations of satellites used for computing the navigation solution for all epochs (for each satellite, all satellites can be used or only some of them when computing the navigation solution).&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>Stanford-ESA</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="3" column="3">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateSBASIonoComponents">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: SBAS Ionospheric Components&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;SBAS Ionospheric Components&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print a component used in the computation of the SBAS Ionosphere as a function of time. By default, it selects the &lt;b&gt;Slant Delay&lt;/b&gt; (the total ionosphere correction applied to the satellite), but it can easily be chosen which model to print, by choosing it in the &lt;i&gt;Y Column&lt;/i&gt; option.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>SBAS Ionospheric Components</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="3" column="2">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateSBASSigmaComponents">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: SBAS Sigma Components&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;SBAS Sigma Components&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print a component of the SBAS sigmas as a function of time. By default, it selects the &lt;b&gt;Total Sigma&lt;/b&gt; (the total sigma applied to the satellite after appliying all SBAS corrections), but it can easily be chosen which model to print, by choosing it in the &lt;i&gt;Y Column&lt;/i&gt; option.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>SBAS Sigma Components</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="3" column="1">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateSBASModelComponents">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: SBAS Model Components&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;SBAS Model Components&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print a component of the SBAS modelling as a function of time. By default, it selects the &lt;b&gt;Pseudorange correction&lt;/b&gt;, but it can easily be chosen which model to print, by choosing it in the &lt;i&gt;Y Column&lt;/i&gt; option.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>SBAS Model Components</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="1" column="3">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonVerStanfordPlot">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Vertical Stanford Plot&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Vertical Stanford Plot&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the Stanford Plot for the Vertical component.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; The Stanford Plot is a heatmap, where each coordinate (being the X axis the positioning error and the Y axis the protection level) represents the number of occurrences in the navigation solution of each combination of positioning error and protection level. With this plot, it is easy to see if there was any occurrence where the positioning error was equal or greater than the protection level.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>Vertical Stanford Plot</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="1" column="2">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonHorStanfordPlot">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: Horizontal Stanford Plot&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;Horizontal Stanford Plot&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the Stanford Plot for the horizontal component.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; The Stanford Plot is a heatmap, where each coordinate (being the X axis the positioning error and the Y axis the protection level) represents the number of occurrences in the navigation solution of each combination of positioning error and protection level. With this plot, it is easy to see if there was any occurrence where the positioning error was equal or greater than the protection level.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>Horizontal Stanford Plot</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="1" column="1">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateVplVpeSat">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: VPE + VPL + #SAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;VPE + VPL + #SAT&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the vertical positioning error (VPE) and vertical protection level (VPL), along with the number of satellites used to compute the navigation solution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This plot is useful to compare the vertical component of the error obtained in the navigation solution with the estimation of the error (the protection level) given by the SBAS provider.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>VPE + VPL + #SAT</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                      <item row="1" column="0">
                       <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButtonTemplateHplHpeSat">
                        <property name="minimumSize">
                         <size>
                          <width>0</width>
                          <height>30</height>
                         </size>
                        </property>
                        <property name="toolTip">
                         <string>&lt;b&gt;Templates: HPE + HPL + #SAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The templates are a set of preconfigured plotting options for the &lt;i&gt;Graphic Details&lt;/i&gt; section. Clicking on any button will load the options in that section, allowing to modify them or plot them directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;i&gt;HPE + HPL + #SAT&lt;/i&gt; template sets the options to print the horizontal positioning error (HPE) and horizontal protection level (HPL), along with the number of satellites used to compute the navigation solution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This plot is useful to compare the horizontal component of the error obtained in the navigation solution with the estimation of the error (the protection level) given by the SBAS provider.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>HPE + HPL + #SAT</string>
                        </property>
                        <property name="default">
                         <bool>true</bool>
                        </property>
                       </widget>
                      </item>
                     </layout>
                    </widget>
                   </item>
                  </layout>
                 </widget>
