                           <property name="toolTip">
                            <string>&lt;b&gt;X Column&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This allows to specify the column for the x values for the selected plot. The combo box will be updated by the &lt;i&gt;First condition&lt;/i&gt;, but the text part is the one that matters. As in the conditions, you can specify several things. In general if you want to plot a column you can do it by putting its column position, such as: &lt;i&gt;4&lt;/i&gt;. You can also use the $4 to plot the forth column. As before, you can do operations between scalars and columns (and even use functions), such as: ($9*2-$1F1*3-1.5). Use the templates buttons to obtain some examples.&lt;br&gt;</string>
