                        <string>When comparing &lt;b&gt;two SP3&lt;/b&gt; orbit files, applying the satellite phase center correction to both files is useless, as the applied correction will dissapear when computing the difference of the satellite positions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The utility of applying the satellite phase center correction is when one of the SP3 files is referred to the satellite mass center (which needs phase center correction), and the other file has been generated from a brodcast file (or other sources, as SP3 file format is easy to generate) whose satellite positions are referred to the antenna phase center (no correction needed).&lt;br&gt;</string>
