                  </size>
                 </property>
                 <property name="toolTip">
                  <string>&lt;b&gt;GLONASS RINEX Navigation File:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Selects the input RINEX navigation file for GLONASS.&lt;br&gt; In order to process GLONASS carrier phase measurements (carrier phase unit is cycles), it is needed the frequency number assigned to each satellite (for converting from meters to cycles), as each satellite uses a different frequency (which is referred to a central frequency).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;These frequency offset are also provided in the header of RINEX observation files (since version 3.02). Alternatively, an optional RINEX navigation can be provided in order to gather these numbers from the GLONASS navigation messages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RINEX navigation files can be found in the links provided in the following menu:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0000FF&quot;&gt;Help-&gt;Download data files-&gt;RINEX Navigation Files&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; Every time a RINEX observation header is read and it contains GLONASS frequency offsets, the frequency offsets will be updated.&lt;br&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="styleSheet">
                  <string notr="true">color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>GLONASS RINEX Nav. File:</string>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
